('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 321, 'cheer', '/cheer: You cheer wildly.\n/cheer self: You cheer for yourself! YAY ME!!\n/cheer target: YAY!! You cheer for (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 322, 'chestpound', '/chestpound: You pound on your chest!\n/chestpound self: You pound on your chest, daring anyone to take you on.\n/chestpound target: You pound your chest. Will (target name) take you on?'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 323, 'chestpuff', '/chestpuff: You puff up your chest and attempt to look imposing.\n/chestpuff self: You chest-puff and pump up your own ego a bit.\n/chestpuff target: You realize that (target name) is just chest-puffing and let (him, her, or it) know that (he, she or it) full of hot air.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 324, 'choppedliver', '/choppedliver: You wonder what is wrong with you. Are you chopped liver?\n/choppedliver self: What am I? Chopped liver?\n/choppedliver target: You ask (target name) if you are chopped liver?'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 325, 'chortle', '/chortle: You chortle.\n/chortle self: With a series of nasally snorts, you chortle to yourself.\n/chortle target: You chortle uncontrollably at the sight of (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 326, 'chuckle', '/chuckle: You chuckle.\n/chuckle self: You chuckle to yourself.\n/chuckle target: You chuckle politely at (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 327, 'city_map', 'If the Politician is a Mayor, he can register his city on the planetary map and register the city''s civic buildings with the /find command.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 328, 'city_spec_cloning', 'The cost of clone insurance in a city with the ''Clone Lab'' specialization is reduced by 20%.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 329, 'city_spec_doctor', 'Medical healing is 10% more effective in a ''Medical Center''.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 330, 'city_spec_entertainer', 'Entertainer healing is 10% more effective in an ''Entertainment District''.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 331, 'city_spec_industry', 'Crafting done in a ''Manufacturing Center'' earns a 10% bonus to prototype assembly results, significantly reducing the chance of failures.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 332, 'city_spec_master_healing', 'A ''Scientific Society'' gains the bonuses of both the ''Medical Center'' and ''Entertainment District'' specializations.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 333, 'city_spec_master_manufacturing', 'An ''Industrial Society'' gains the bonuses of both the ''Manufacturing Center'' and ''Research Center'' specializations.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 334, 'city_spec_missions', 'Missions taken in a city with an ''Improved Job Market'' grant a 15% increase to their rewards.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 335, 'city_spec_research', 'Any experimentation done within a ''Research Center'' is enhanced.  A 15% bonus to the final result roll is added during the experimentation phase of crafting.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 336, 'city_spec_sample_rich', 'A sample rich city has a lot of highly accessable surface resources for manual collection.  The sample rich city bestows a 20% bonus to sample sizes and a 10% bonus to extraction skill checks during resource collection using a survey tool.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 337, 'city_spec_stronghold', 'A ''Stronghold'' has trained its militia members to the peak of their abilities in the methods of tactical defense.  Militia members in a ''Stronghold'' get a 50 point bonus to all defense rolls against other players.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 338, 'cityban', '/cityban <target>: Prevents a player from being able to buy travel tickets at the city shuttleport and prevents them from entering public civic structures like cloning facilities and the city hall.  You may only use this command if you are a militia member.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 339, 'citypardon', '/citypardon <target>: Removes the ban state from a person in your city.  You may only use this command if you are a militia member.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 340, 'citywarn', '/citywarn <target>: Warns the target to leave the city in 30 seconds or be attacked.  Players made attackable with this command cannot defend themselves, but are only attackable up to the city limits.  You may only use this command if you are a militia member.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 341, 'clap', '/clap: You clap your hands together.\n/clap self: You give yourself a hand.\n/clap target: You clap for (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 342, 'claw', '/claw: You hiss and bare your claws.\n/claw self: You remove a file from your pack and begin to sharpen your claws.\n/claw target: You claw at (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 343, 'close', '/close: You close your eyes for a moment.\n/close self: You close your eyes for a moment, thinking.\n/close target: You close your eyes, unwilling to look at (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 344, 'closeeyes', '/closeeyes:  You close your eyes for a moment.\n/closeeyes self:  You close your eyes for a moment, thinking.\n/closeeyes target:  You close your eyes, unwilling to look at (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 345, 'colorlights', '/colorlights: Performs a series of colored light effects.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 346, 'comb', '/comb: Looking for something? You comb the area.\n/comb self: You comb your hair. There! Perfect!\n/comb target: You comb (target name)''s hair.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 347, 'combarea', '/combarea:  Looking for something? You comb the area.\n/combarea self:  There you are!\n/combarea target:  You comb the area searching for (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 348, 'combattarget', '/combattarget:  Type /combattarget while on an attackable target to maintain that as what you will be attacking, regardless of what else you target afterwards.  This is very useful for healing other party members while fighting creatures or players.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 349, 'combhair', '/combhair:  You claw at the knots in your hair in desperate need of a comb.\n/combhair self:  You comb your hair. There! Perfect!\n/combhair target:  You comb (target name)''s hair.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 350, 'comfort', '/comfort: You comfort everyone and let them know it will be OK.\n/comfort self: You subtly drop the hint that you could use some comforting.\n/comfort target: You comfort (him, her, or it).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 351, 'con', '/con'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 352, 'conceal', '/conceal: This command allows you to apply a camouflage kit to become far less detectable by NPCs and creatures while in the concealed state.  This can be used on other players.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 353, 'concealshot', '/concealshot <target>: This ranged sneak attack, if successful, will damage your target without them knowing where the attack came from.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 354, 'confusionshot', '/confusionshot <target>: This ranged attack is designed to confuse its target, and can stun and dizzy its target as well.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 355, 'congratulate', '/congratulate: Congrats to all!\n/congratulate self: You give yourself a pat on the back.\n/congratulate target: You congratulate (him, her, or it).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 356, 'consent', '/consent'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 357, 'consider', '/consider: This allows you to determine the relative difficulty of your current target.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 358, 'contemplate', '/contemplate: You contemplate.\n/contemplate self: You contemplate your future.\n/contemplate target: You contemplate (target name)''s future.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 359, 'corpse', '/corpse: Using this command with a corpse targeted will move the corpse closer to you.  If it is not your corpse, you will need /consent from the player who died.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 360, 'cough', '/cough: *COUGH* *COUGH*\n/cough self: *cough* *ahem* You hack out a stifled cough. Trying to tell someone something?\n/cough target: You cough in (his, her, or its) face.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 361, 'counterattack', 'This command utilizes the counter attack sequence.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 362, 'cover', '/cover: You tell everyone to cover up!\n/cover self: Feeling a draft?\n/cover target: Get some clothes on (target name)!'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 363, 'covereyes', '/covereyes: You cover your eyes.\n/covereyes self: You hide your eyes behind your crossed arms.\n/covereyes target: You cover (his, her, or its) eyes.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 364, 'cower', '/cower: You cower.\n/cower self: You cower submissively.\n/cower target: You cower away from (him, her, or it).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 365, 'createmanfschematic', 'This command is used to create a manufacture schematic.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 366, 'createprototype', 'This command allows the user to create a prototype.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 367, 'creatureareableeding', 'Creature'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 368, 'creatureareacombo', 'Creatures'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 369, 'creatureareadisease', 'Creature'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 370, 'creatureareaknockdown', 'Creatures'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 371, 'creatureareapoison', 'Creature'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 372, 'creatureareattack', 'Creatures'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 373, 'cringe', '/cringe: EEP! You cringe.\n/cringe self: You cringe at the thought.\n/cringe target: You cringe away from (target name) in fear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 374, 'cripplingshot', '/cripplingshot <target>: This powerful ranged attack is very damaging to a single target.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 375, 'cry', '/cry: You burst into tears.\n/cry self: You cry uncontrollably.\n/cry target: You cry on (his, her, or its) shoulder.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 376, 'cu', '/cu: See ya later.\n/cu self: "Not if I see you first!"\n/cu target: See ya later, (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 377, 'cuckoo', '/cuckoo: These people are cuckoo.\n/cuckoo self: You just realized that you are cuckoo.\n/cuckoo target: You think (target name) is cuckoo.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 378, 'culater', '/culater:  See ya later.\n/culater self:  "Not if I see you first!"\n/culater target:  See ya later, (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 379, 'curedisease', '/curedisease <target>: This command enables you to cure disease from a target, if you have the appropriate medical equipment.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 380, 'curepoison', '/curepoison <target>: This command enables you to cure poison from a target, if you have the appropriate medical equipment.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 381, 'curious', '/curious: You look around inquisitively.\n/curious self: You look curiously at yourself, as if something has changed.\n/curious target: You peer curiously over (his, her, or its) shoulder.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 382, 'curse', '/curse: You spew obscenities.\n/curse self: You quietly curse to yourself.\n/curse target: You spew obscenities at (target name), and let (him, her, or it) have it.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 383, 'curtsey', '/curtsey: You curtsey for your audience.\n/curtsey self: You perform a very formal curtsey.\n/curtsey target: You curtsey to (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 384, 'customizedroid', 'This command allows the user to attempt to customize the target droid.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 385, 'dance', '/dance: You dance about the area.\n/dance self: You dance with yourself.\n/dance target: You grab (target name) and drag (him, her, or it) to the dance-floor.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 386, 'dancer', 'This ability allows you to perform dance commands.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 387, 'dazzle', '/dazzle: Performs a dazzling effect of color and lights.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 388, 'declareovert', 'This command allows a covert faction member to declare overt faction status. Usage of this command is restricted to a 50m radius around friendly player-placed faction headquarters.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 389, 'deepbow', '/deepbow: You bow deeply.\n/deepbow self: You bow deeply before yourself and almost fall over.\n/deepbow target: You bow deeply before (target name), showing great respect.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 390, 'defaultattack', 'This is the most basic attack action.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 391, 'defend', '/defend: You try to stand imposingly, exhibiting your intent to defend the area.\n/defend self: You prepare to defend yourself.\n/defend target: You step in front of (target name), ready to defend (him, her, or it).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 392, 'defuseminefield', 'This command allows the user to defuse a mine field.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 393, 'demure', '/demure: You blush shyly.\n/demure self: You blush, smiling secretly.\n/demure target: You blush shyly at (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 394, 'deride', '/deride: Playing the town fool? You ridicule everyone about you.\n/deride self: You deride yourself.\n/deride target: You laugh at (target name) with contempt.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 395, 'diagnose', '/diagnose: This ability reveals the attribute wounds of your target so that you can focus your healing efforts where they are most needed. The wounds shown are a snapshot of your target at the time you diagnose them. If you wish to update your target''s wound information to reflect recent healing or damage, simply diagnose them again.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 396, 'dies', '/dies: Death to all of them!\n/dies self: You contemplate the meaning of life.\n/dies target: You grimly dictate the fate of (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 397, 'disagree', '/disagree: You politely disagree.\n/disagree self: You change your mind and disagree with your last statement.\n/disagree target: You disagree with (target name).'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 398, 'disarmingshot1', '/disarmingshot1 <target>: This ranged attack is used to hit your opponent''s weapon.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 399, 'disarmingshot2', '/disarmingshot2 <target>: This ranged attack is used to hit your opponent''s weapon.  This is more powerful than Disarming Shot 1.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 400, 'dismiss', '/dismiss: You dismiss everyone.\n/dismiss self: You dismiss the notion.\n/dismiss target: You dismiss (target name) with a quick gesture.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 401, 'dismount', '/dismount: You climb down of your mount, if you are currently on one.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 402, 'distract', '/distract: Performs a distracting effect of color and lights.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 403, 'diveshot', '/diveshot: A diving shot will cause you to dive and attack at the same time, leaving you in a prone position.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 404, 'dizzyattack', 'This command utilizes the dizzy attack.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 405, 'dock', '/dock: Dock with or undock from a space station.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 406, 'doh', '/doh: Doh!\n/doh self: DOH DOH DOH!\n/doh target: You look at (him, her, or it) and say "DOH!"'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 407, 'doubletap', '/doubletap <target>: This ranged attack fires two bolts at once, damaging your target more than the default attack.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 408, 'down', '/down: You point at the ground.\n/down self: You''re staying right here!\n/down target: You tell (target name) to stay right here.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 409, 'dragincapacitatedplayer', '/dragincapacitatedplayer <target>: This command allows you to drag an incapacitated player to a safer location than where they became incapacitated at.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 410, 'dragplayer', '/dragplayer <name>: This command allows you to drag an incapacitated player to safety.  It functions similarly to the /corpse command, in that you must be somewhat close for this command to work.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 411, 'drainforce', '/drainForce <target>: This attack allows a Jedi to drain stored Force power from another player Jedi.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 412, 'dream', '/dream: You float away on a fluffy white cloud.\n/dream self: Daydreaming again?\n/dream target: Dreamy, isn''t (he, she or it)?'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 413, 'droid+droidcommand_breaklockfour', 'Spoof incoming warheads.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 414, 'droid+droidcommand_breaklockone', 'Spoof incoming warheads.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 415, 'droid+droidcommand_breaklockthree', 'Spoof incoming warheads.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 416, 'droid+droidcommand_breaklocktwo', 'Spoof incoming warheads.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 417, 'droid+droidcommand_engineefficiencyfour', 'Engines consume less power, at the cost of a bit less thrust.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 418, 'droid+droidcommand_engineefficiencyone', 'Engines consume less power, at the cost of a bit less thrust.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 419, 'droid+droidcommand_engineefficiencythree', 'Engines consume less power, at the cost of a bit less thrust.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 420, 'droid+droidcommand_engineefficiencytwo', 'Engines consume less power, at the cost of a bit less thrust.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 421, 'droid+droidcommand_enginenormalize', 'Engine settings to their defaults.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 422, 'droid+droidcommand_engineoverloadfour', 'Makes engines provide more thrust, but is rather wasteful in energy.');
INSERT INTO `client_strings` (`stringFile`, `index`, `name`, `value`) VALUES
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 423, 'droid+droidcommand_engineoverloadone', 'Makes engines provide more thrust, but is rather wasteful in energy.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 424, 'droid+droidcommand_engineoverloadthree', 'Makes engines provide more thrust, but is rather wasteful in energy.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 425, 'droid+droidcommand_engineoverloadtwo', 'Makes engines provide more thrust, but is rather wasteful in energy.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 426, 'droid+droidcommand_mutedroid', 'Toggles off and on the flight droid or flight-computer''s auditory feedback mode, giving the pilot some control over how talkative and responsive they are.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 427, 'droid+droidcommand_reactornormalize', 'Reset reactor back to default settings.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 428, 'droid+droidcommand_reactoroverloadfour', 'Reactor to generate more energy, at the cost of over-stressing it.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 429, 'droid+droidcommand_reactoroverloadone', 'Reactor to generate more energy, at the cost of over-stressing it.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 430, 'droid+droidcommand_reactoroverloadthree', 'Reactor to generate more energy, at the cost of over-stressing it.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 431, 'droid+droidcommand_reactoroverloadtwo', 'Reactor to generate more energy, at the cost of over-stressing it.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 432, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldadjustfrontfour', 'Changes the shield generators to generate stronger front shields than rear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 433, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldadjustfrontone', 'Changes the shield generators to generate stronger front shields than rear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 434, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldadjustfrontthree', 'Changes the shield generators to generate stronger front shields than rear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 435, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldadjustfronttwo', 'Changes the shield generators to generate stronger front shields than rear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 436, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldadjustrearfour', 'Changes the shield generators to generate stronger rear shields than front.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 437, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldadjustrearone', 'Changes the shield generators to generate stronger rear shields than front.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 438, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldadjustrearthree', 'Changes the shield generators to generate stronger rear shields than front.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 439, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldadjustreartwo', 'Changes the shield generators to generate stronger rear shields than front.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 440, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldbacktofronteighty', 'Divert most of the stored charge from the rear shields to the front.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 441, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldbacktofrontfifty', 'Divert some of the stored charge from the rear shields to the front.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 442, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldbacktofronthundred', 'Divert all of the stored charge from the rear shields to the front.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 443, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldbacktofronttwenty', 'Divert some of the stored charge from the rear shields to the front.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 444, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldemergencyfront', 'This program immediately leeches the majority of rear shield energy and current weapon capacitor charge and diverts it all to the front shield facing. This is an instantaneous command with no lasting effects on any of the ship''s systems involved.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 445, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldemergencyrear', 'This program immediately leeches the majority of front shield energy and current weapon capacitor charge and diverts it all to the rear shield facing. This is an instantaneous command with no lasting effects on any of the ship''s systems involved.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 446, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldfronttobackeighty', 'Divert most of the stored charge from the front shields to the rear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 447, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldfronttobackfifty', 'Divert some of the stored charge from the front shields to the rear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 448, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldfronttobackhundred', 'Divert all of the stored charge from the front shields to the rear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 449, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldfronttobacktwenty', 'Divert some of the stored charge from the front shields to the rear.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 450, 'droid+droidcommand_shieldnormalize', 'Resets shields back to their defaults.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 451, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcapequalize', 'Resets the weapon capacitor energy settings back to their defaults.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 452, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcappowerupfour', 'Tell the droid to run more power through the weapon capacitor than it is rated for, leading to enhanced performance.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 453, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcappowerupone', 'Tell the droid to run more power through the weapon capacitor than it is rated for, leading to enhanced performance.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 454, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcappowerupthree', 'Tell the droid to run more power through the weapon capacitor than it is rated for, leading to enhanced performance.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 455, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcappoweruptwo', 'Tell the droid to run more power through the weapon capacitor than it is rated for, leading to enhanced performance.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 456, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcaptoshieldfour', 'This program allows the droid to use back-up power-routing systems to shunt power currently stored in the weapon capacitor directly to the shield generator systems.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 457, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcaptoshieldone', 'This program allows the droid to use back-up power-routing systems to shunt power currently stored in the weapon capacitor directly to the shield generator systems.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 458, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcaptoshieldthree', 'This program allows the droid to use back-up power-routing systems to shunt power currently stored in the weapon capacitor directly to the shield generator systems.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 459, 'droid+droidcommand_weapcaptoshieldtwo', 'This program allows the droid to use back-up power-routing systems to shunt power currently stored in the weapon capacitor directly to the shield generator systems.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 460, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponeffeciencyfour', 'Re-tune the weapons to use less power, at the cost of performance.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 461, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponeffeciencyone', 'Re-tune the weapons to use less power, at the cost of performance.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 462, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponeffeciencythree', 'Re-tune the weapons to use less power, at the cost of performance.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 463, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponeffeciencytwo', 'Re-tune the weapons to use less power, at the cost of performance.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 464, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponnormalize', 'Reset the weapon power to defaults.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 465, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponoverload1', 'This command will increase the damage out put of your weapons by 25%. It will increase the energy requirements as well.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 466, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponoverloadfour', 'Increase weapon performance, at the cost of effeciency and possible system stress.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 467, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponoverloadone', 'Increase weapon performance, at the cost of effeciency and possible system stress.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 468, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponoverloadthree', 'Increase weapon performance, at the cost of effeciency and possible system stress.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 469, 'droid+droidcommand_weaponoverloadtwo', 'Increase weapon performance, at the cost of effeciency and possible system stress.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 470, 'droid_find', 'This Bounty Hunter innate ability enables your probe droid to indicate to you where you should go next to find your quarry.'),
('string/en/cmd_d.stf', 471, 'droid_track', 'This advanced Bounty Hunter innate ability enables you to receive a continual update on where your probe droid is indicating your quarry has recently been.'),
