('string/en/frn_d.stf', 145, 'painting_trees_s01', 'In the tradition of Life Day, this painting depicts the landscape of the Wookiee homeworld Kashyyyk. It was probably painted by memory as part of a Life Day remembrance ceremony.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 146, 'painting_twilek_f', 'A portrait of a female Twi''lek.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 147, 'painting_twilek_m', 'This painting was done by Furva Keill, and was supposedly inspired by his dealings with Bib Fortuna, Jabba the Hutt''s major domo.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 148, 'painting_vet_01', 'Cast Wing in Flight, given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 149, 'painting_vet_02', 'Decimator, given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 150, 'painting_vet_03', 'Tatooine Dune Speeder, given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 151, 'painting_vet_04', 'Weapon of War, given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 152, 'painting_vet_05', 'Fighter Study, given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 153, 'painting_vet_06', 'Hutt Greed, given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 154, 'painting_vet_07', 'Smuggler''s Run, given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 155, 'painting_vet_08', 'Imperial Oppression (TIE Oppressor), given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 156, 'painting_vet_09', 'Emperor''s Eyes (TIE Sentinel), given for the one year anniversary of Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 157, 'painting_wookiee_f', 'In the tradition of Life Day, this painting represents a family matriarch who has passed away.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 158, 'painting_wookiee_m', 'In the tradition of Life Day, this painting represents a family patriarch who has passed away.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 159, 'painting_zabrak_f', 'A portrait of Lady T''Inia, the wife of a Zabrak warrior of some reknown.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 160, 'painting_zabrak_m', 'A portrait of High Commander T''Inia, recently commissioned for a Zabrak warrior of some reknown.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 161, 'park_bench', 'This is a bench, like the kind you''d find in a park.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 162, 'pitcher_full', 'This is a pitcher full of liquid.  Probably water.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 163, 'plain_bowl', 'This is a plain bowl.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 164, 'portable_stove', 'This is a small portable stove.  Though it has all its components it doesn''t appear to work.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 165, 'radio', 'This is a radio.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 166, 'sarlacc', 'The Sarlacc is a gruesome, omnivorous, immobile beast almost entirely concealed beneath the desert sands. Only its foul mouth extends to the surface, ringed with grasping tentacles ready to pull any prey unfortunate to fall into the shifting sands. Because of its isolation, the Sarlacc rarely feeds, as it must rely on animals that stumble into the pit. As such, it has evolved an extremely efficient digestive process. According to lore, the stomach pit of the Sarlacc keeps its prey alive for a thousand years, slowly dissolving its meal into needed nutrients, while the hapless victim is kept alive in searing, endless agony. '),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 167, 'shisa', 'A shisa.  Like the one in Jabba''s Palace.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 168, 'skeleton_human', 'A human skeleton.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 169, 'skyscraper', 'A blueprint poster of a skyscraper to be built on Coronet.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 170, 'slave_brazier', 'This is a decorative brazier.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 171, 'spear_rack', 'A decorative rack of weapons.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 172, 'squill_lair', 'A squill lair. Upon further investigation, you can see a skull inside. The skull seems as if it would be important to someone. Maybe you can search it somehow?'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 173, 'starmap', 'A stylized painting of a starmap.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 174, 'stuffed_fish', 'This is a fished, stuffed, meant to be used as a display item.  Apparently someone thinks they''re quite the fisherman...'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 175, 'tanning_hide', 'This is a stretched leather hide, used as a decoration.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 176, 'tatooine_tapestry', 'This is a tapestry with a symbol for Tatooine on it.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 177, 'teras_kasi', 'This is a poster for a Teras Kasi attack known as the "Spitting Rawl Technique"'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 178, 'teras_kasi_2', 'This is a poster for a classic Teras Kasi defensive stance.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 179, 'trandoshan_wanted', 'This is a wanted poster for a Trandoshan who has committed atrocities against a Wookiee clan.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 180, 'vader_victory', 'A poster of Lord Darth Vader, with the text "Victory through Conform"'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 181, 'valley_view', 'This is a landscape of a view through a valley.'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 182, 'victorious_reign', 'This is a propaganda poster showing a Stormtrooper with the text "Victorious Reign"'),
('string/en/frn_d.stf', 183, 'waterfall', 'This is a knock-off or a forgery of an actual painting of the Agrilat region.'),
