('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 28, 'expel_shield', 'You are pushed back by an invisible force!  You suspect some sort of shield technology is involved.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 29, 'shield_remote_interference', 'There is too much electronic interference for this device to work here.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 30, 'shield_remote_cant_use', 'You don''t know how to operate this particular remote control model.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 31, 'shield_remote_wrong_camp', 'The lights on the remote flicker briefly, but nothing happens.  This remote must use an incorrect frequency for this camp.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 32, 'remote_nothing_happens', 'Nothing happens.  You must be closter to the enemy camp shield generator for that too work.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 33, 'remote_shield_down_already', 'Althought your remote has the correct frequency for this shield generator, the shield generator has already been powered down by someone else.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 34, 'remote_shield_down_by_player', 'Althought your remote has the correct frequency for this shield generator, the shield generator has already been powered down by %TT.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 35, 'remote_powering_down', 'The shield generator appears to be powering down.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 36, 'camp_defender_1', 'INTRUDERS!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 37, 'camp_defender_2', 'Find the intruders and slay them!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 38, 'camp_defender_3', 'We are under attack!  Spread out!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 39, 'camp_defender_4', 'I shall defend my commander until the death!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 40, 'camp_defender_5', 'ATTAAAACK!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 41, 'camp_defender_6', 'The commander has called in reinforcements.  Hold off the intruders until they arrive!!!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 42, 'camp_defender_7', 'Hold the line!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 43, 'camp_defender_8', 'Defend the base!  Don''t let the intruders slip inside!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 44, 'camp_defender_9', 'You will have to get past me first, scum!'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 45, 'camp_defender_10', 'Running is futile!  You will only die tired.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 47, 'remote_detail', 'This device looks like it has been contructed by an amateur.  There is no telling how well it might work.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 48, 'remote_name', 'a shield generator remote'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 49, 'crystal_name', 'a frequence resonance crystal'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 50, 'crystal_detail', 'this resonance crystal must be combined with the correct frequence crystal cache to be of any use'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 51, 'cache_name', 'a resonance crystal cache'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 52, 'cache_detail', 'This crystal caches is used to store frequence resonance crystals - often used in various remote control technologies.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 53, 'fs_cs_intro_journal_sum', 'Capture Enemy Leadership'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 54, 'fs_cs_intro_journal_detail', 'With several enemy camps on Dathomir, Captain Sarguillo of the Aurilian village has asked you to scout out the locations of these camps.  They could be located anywhere on Dathomir.  Each camp has a shield generator that must be powered down remotely before you can infiltrate the camp.  In order to find the frequency codes for the various shield generators in use at the enemy camps, you must hunt down members of the enemy force and relieve them of any frequence code datadisks they might be carrying.  If you return such a datadisk to Captain Sarguillo, he will give you a remote control configured for the frequency code on the disk.  You may then use this remote to power down the corresponding shield. \n\nOnce you have a remote control device (or you are grouped with someone who has one),  you may attempt to capture the camp''s commander.   There are two ways to earn credit for this mission:\n\nOption 1:  Power down the shield generator and eliminate at least 5 of the enemy''s troops afterwards - that should be enough to lure the commander out.  You will also be made personally responsible for making sure the commander gets back safely to Aurilia.  If you perish any time after the shield comes down but before the commander is captured, i.e. you will need to complete ''Option 2'' below, instead of allowing one of your group mates to take on that responsibility. \n\nOption 2:  Join a group with someone who powered down the shield generator and capture the commander.  You must then safely return him to Captain Sarguillo for questioning. \n\nSince the Aurilians value teamwork and comraderie so greatly, you will receive a mission bonus from Captain Sarguillo if you complete this mission with a friend.  To become eligible for the bonus, one of you must power down the shield and one of you must capture the commander. \n\nRemember that the mission is not complete for any participant until the commander is safely returned to the Aurilian village.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 55, 'fs_cs_kill_guards_sum', 'Kill 5 Enemy Troops'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 56, 'fs_cs_kill_guards_detail', 'Kill at least 5 of the camp''s defending troops and stay alive until the commander has been captured.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 57, 'fs_cs_primary_escort_detail', 'You have taken custody of the base commander.  Being a well-trained agent of the Dark Side, he has ingested a quantity of biotoxins in an attempt to end his own life before being captured and interrogated.  Make haste and return the commander to the village before the toxins take their toll on him.  Without medical attention from the Aurilian healers, he will not live to see the interrogation chambers.  You have less than an hour to return him to the village.\n\nIf the commander is not safely returned to the village, no one who has participated in the mission will receive credit.  If you lose custody of the commander, you will lose this mission.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 58, 'fs_cs_primary_escort_sum', 'Return the Commander to Aurilia'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 59, 'fs_cs_secondary_escort_sum', 'Escort the Commander to Aurilia'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 60, 'fs_cs_secondary_escort_detail', 'The commander has been captured by someone in your group.  You must ensure that he is delivered to Aurilia safe and sound.  Being a well trained agent of the Dark Side, the commander has ingested a quantity of bio toxins in an attempt to end his own life before being captured and interrogated.  If he is not returned to the village for immediate medical attention he will surely perish and your efforts will have been in vain.\n\nIf the commander does not make it to the village, you will not receive credit for this mission.  Should something unspeakable happen to your party member and they can no longer retain custody of the commander, you may recapture the commander if you can catch up with him.  This way you can still receive credit for the mission, even if your partner fails.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 61, 'fs_cs_accepted', 'You have accepted the mission.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 62, 'waypoint_datapad_name', 'a waypoint datapad'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 63, 'waypoint_datapad_detail', 'This datapad appears to contain coordinates for some sort of outpost.  The records mention something about shadow of the Sith.'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 64, 'frequency_datapad_name', 'remote frequency codes'),
('string/en/fs_quest_village.stf', 65, 'frequency_datapad_detail', 'This datapad appears to contain frequency codes for a shield generator.  Return it to Captain Sarguillo at the Aurilian village on Dathomir for more information.'),
