('string/en/loading/dathomir.stf', 1, 'rancor', 'Part crustacean, part arachnid, the Rancor is a beast native to Dathomir.\n\nIt is covered in knobby, natural armor and bony headplates.  Its claws, teeth, and massive size are what make the Rancor legendary.\n\nSome people have been known to keep Rancors as pets, whereas the Witches of Dathomir respect them for what they truly are.'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir.stf', 2, 'dathomir', 'Home to outcasts from the Republic, the mighty rancor and the force-sensitive Nightsisters, Dathomir is a dangerous planet where few survive for any period of time.'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir.stf', 3, 'imperial_prison', 'Dathomir is home to an Imperial Prison, where the Empire will send criminals meant to be forgotten (and they frequently are).'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir.stf', 4, 'singing_mountain_clan', 'Enemies of the Night Sisters, the Singing Mountain clan are a group of force-sensitive people. People who have seen the home of the Singing Mountain Clan return with strange reports of unusual sights.'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir.stf', 5, 'trade_outpost', 'A few, tiny outposts have successfully established residence on Dathomir.  One, the trade outpost, is the common location for wary travelers to this dangerous planet.  Trade in Dathomir goods is usually based on a few rare resources that are unique to Dathomir, as well as infant creatures that can potentially be tamed.'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir_n.stf', 1, 'rancor', 'Rancor'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir_n.stf', 2, 'dathomir', 'Dathomir'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir_n.stf', 3, 'imperial_prison', 'Imperial Prison'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir_n.stf', 4, 'singing_mountain_clan', 'Singing Mountain Clan'),
('string/en/loading/dathomir_n.stf', 5, 'trade_outpost', 'Trade Outpost'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 1, 'hanadak', 'The hanadak looks like a cross between a large primate and a common boar, yet enlarged in all of its proportions.\n\nHaving a fondness for meat, many a traveler to Endor has learned that the hanadak are as frightening as they appear to be.\n\nSome of the sentient species on the planet claim that the giant gorax are actually the true masters of the hanadak.\n'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 2, 'blurrg', 'Inhabiting the savannas of the Forest Moon of Endor, the blurrg is a remarkably stupid creature that has been domesticated by the Marauders. '),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 3, 'condor_dragon', 'The condor dragon, or mantigrue, is a large flighted lizard on the Forest Moon of Endor. They are often aggressive and can be quite dangerous.'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 4, 'lantern_bird', 'A beautiful flying creature from the Forest Moon of Endor, the lantern bird is notable for its brilliant plumage. '),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 5, 'merek', 'Half-arachnid and half-monkey, the merek is a strange creature native to the Forest Moon of Endor. They do not live in families, generally, and are not particularly aggressive in the wild.'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 6, 'remmer', 'Natives of the Forest Moon of Endor, remmer are disgusting little scavenger creatures. They eat practically everything: dirt, string, carrion, wood, paper, bugs...'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 7, 'swirl_prong', 'Commonly found alone or in small groups, the swirl prong of Endor easily navigates steep cliffs in order to stay away from predators. If need be, they will use their horns to defend themselves.'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 8, 'gorax', 'A gigantic monster native to the Forest Moon of Endor, the gorax preys on Ewoks, since it is tall enough to reach directly into their treetop homes.'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 9, 'dulok', 'The "dark form" of the Ewoks, the Duloks are ill-proportioned cousins featuring fangs and large, pointed ears. Like the Ewoks, they are also native to the Forest Moon of Endor.'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 10, 'ewok', 'A small race of furry humanoids, the Ewoks are the primary native civilization on the Forest Moon of Endor. They live in treetop villages, or in some cases, in homes built on stilts by the lakeshores.\n\nAlthough they lack high technology, they are intelligent and cunning.'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 11, 'marauder', 'Long ago, a reptilian species was stranded on the Forest Moon of Endor. These Marauders, as they are known, have been living there ever since, attacking visitors to the planet. A warlike society, they scavenge any technology they can find.'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 12, 'lake_villages', 'Some tribes of Ewoks built lake villages, with unique conical structures on stilts built over the water.'),
('string/en/loading/endor.stf', 13, 'tree_villages', 'Most Ewok tribes that dwell in the forest build their homes in the trees themselves. These villages are accessed via ramps and rope ladders.'),
('string/en/loading/endor_n.stf', 1, 'hanadak', 'Hanadak\n'),
