('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 1, 'gig_mission_dance_start', 'Follow the waypoint to your local cantina, go inside and dance for 2 minutes.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 2, 'gig_mission_music_start', 'Follow the waypoint to your local cantina, go inside and play a song for 2 minutes.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 3, 'gig_mission_arrival', 'You''ve arrived at the cantina, go inside and start your performance.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 4, 'survey_mission_start', 'Use your survey tool to locate a XX% density patch of blah, a type of suchandsuch.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 5, 'destroy_mission_start', 'Follow the waypoint to target and destroy it.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 6, 'gig_mission_complete', 'You have completed your sample Gig Mission.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 7, 'survey_mission_complete', 'You have completed your sample Survey Mission.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 8, 'destroy_mission_complete', 'You have completed your sample Destroy Mission'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 9, 'heal_mission_start', 'Follow the waypoint to %TT and use the given medicine to heal %OT.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 10, 'heal_mission_arrival', 'You have found your patient, start healing %OT as soon as possible.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 11, 'heal_mission_complete', 'You have sucessfully healed your patient.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 12, 'harvest_mission_start', 'Follow the waypoint to your target and kill it.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 13, 'harvest_mission_target_dead', 'Now that your target is dead, use your skills to harvest the natural resources from it.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 14, 'harvest_mission_complete', 'You have sucessfully harvested resources from your target.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 15, 'heal_mission_menu', 'Heal Patient'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 16, 'heal_mission_use', 'Use Medicine'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 17, 'heal_mission_need_target', 'You need to have a target to use this medicine.'),
('string/en/newbie_handoff/messages.stf', 18, 'heal_mission_wrong_target', 'This is not the correct patient.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 1, 'greeting', 'A straggler, eh?  Don''t be shy, come on forward.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 2, 'explain_lookat', 'Well, I have things for you, but I won''t give you the time of day unless you actually converse with me.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 5, 'convo_1_start', 'That''s more like it.  Well, I''m your supply disbursement officer.  I don''t see why we should waste good supplies on refugees like you.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 6, 'convo_1_reply_1', 'What happened?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 7, 'convo_1_reply_2', 'What supplies?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 8, 'convo_1_more', 'You people, you''re all the same. Look, you were on a ship with dubious credentials. The Star Destroyer hailed you, and you didn''t stop fast enough. So they boarded, and brought the survivors over here.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 11, 'convo_1_stuff', 'There''s some stuff left that the other refugees didn''t take. Not much though. In the drum right here.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 12, 'clone_greeting', 'Well hello!  Please allow me to answer any questions that you might have.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 13, 'clone_prompt_convo', 'Remember, to speak to me just click-and-hold on me until you get the radial menu, then select the CONVERSE menu option.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 14, 'convo_2_start', 'I''m here to explain Cloning and Insurance.  Where would you like to begin?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 15, 'convo_2_reply_1', 'Cloning'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 16, 'convo_2_reply_2', 'Insurance.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 17, 'convo_2_cloning', 'If something should happen to you, your clone will take over with all the skills you had at the time you died.  Though you always have the option to respawn at the nearest cloning facility, unless you''ve cloned there you will emerge with many, many wounds.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 18, 'convo_2_reply_3', 'How often should I clone?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 19, 'convo_2_insurance', 'Insurance is a way of better preserving the condition of your belongings in the event of your untimely demise.  The return of nominally damaged, insured items to a cloning facility fetches a much higher price with the facility at which you choose to clone since you subsidize their item retrieval programs by purchasing insurance.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 20, 'convo_2_reply_4', 'What happens to uninsured items?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 21, 'convo_2_cloning_2', 'You should clone yourself whenever you want the option to emerge from that particular location. Otherwise you will appear at the closest cloning facility from where you died, with many wounds. You will also need to set a new cloning location when you travel to a new planet, because there is no interplanetary cloning.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 22, 'convo_2_reply_5', 'Do I need to clone again every time I die?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 23, 'convo_2_insurance_2', 'Your items will suffer a significantly increased decay rate when transported back to your clone. People like to be paid, and cloning facilities don''t pay much for recovery of uninsured items; so it stands to reason that uninsured items tend to not be cared for as well as their insured counterparts.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 24, 'convo_2_reply_6', 'Running back to my corpse sounds like fun!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 25, 'convo_2_reply_7', 'I hate the idea of running to my corpse!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 26, 'convo_2_cloning_3', 'No.  Only when you want to have the option of appearing at a particular location without a lot of wounds, regardless of where you died.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 27, 'convo_2_reply_8', 'Do I have to insure my items every time I die?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 28, 'convo_2_insurance_3', 'You must like living life on the edge.... or you like travelling.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 29, 'convo_2_insurance_5', 'Yes!  Insurance is only valid one time.  If you want your items returned to you in a condition similar to last you saw them, you''ll have to insure the item again!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 30, 'convo_2_insurance_4', 'I don''t blame you.  It sounds like a real chore.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 31, 'convo_3_explain_terminal_1', 'Use terminals like this one, located in cloning facilities, to store your clone data.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 32, 'convo_3_explain_terminal_2', 'I also have an insurance terminal for you here, where you may insure your items to prevent loss.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 42, 'convo_1_agree', 'There''s nothing to it.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 44, 'banker_greeting', 'Well hello!  Come talk to me if you need assistance with this terminal'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 45, 'banker_1_start', 'Well it seems your ship wasn''t carrying contraband after all.  Pity we didn''t discover that sooner...'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 46, 'banker_1_reply_1', 'What did you do to my ship?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 47, 'banker_1_reply_2', 'What is this terminal for?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 48, 'banker_2_start', 'Well we suspected you were smuggling, so we boarded the transport you were travelling aboard, of course.  Don''t worry, we''ve cleared you of all charges.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 49, 'banker_2_reply_1', 'Can I get back on board the transport now?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 50, 'banker_2_more', 'I''m afraid not.  It seems your ship was badly damaged and most of your possessions were destroyed.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 51, 'banker_2_reply_2', 'What am I supposed to do now?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 52, 'banker_2_explain', 'Don''t worry!  We''ve taken care of everything.  We''ve given you more than enough credits to reimburse you for your loss.  You can deposit them at this banking terminal.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 53, 'banker_2_reply_3', 'What about my supplies and equipment?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 54, 'banker_2_explain_2', 'When you get to a planet, look for a commodities market and buy anything you might possibly need.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 55, 'banker_2_explain_terminals', 'For your convenience, we''ll allow you to access this starport''s bank terminal.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 56, 'banker_1_reply_3', 'Bank?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 57, 'banker_1_reply_4', 'Item dispenser?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 58, 'banker_2_explain_bank', 'Once we realized you were innocent, we reimbursed you with a generous number of credits for the destruction of your gear.  You can deposit them in this bank terminal.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 59, 'banker_bank_reply_1', 'Why should I bank?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 60, 'banker_2_more_bank', 'You should definitely use the bank''s safety deposit feature to keep your items safe from harm. It''s also a good idea to deposit your credits into your bank accout before shopping at the commodities market since the market deducts credits from your bank account for all purchases.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 61, 'banker_2_bank_question', 'What if I want to buy something?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 62, 'banker_2_bank_answer', 'You don''t need cash on hand to buy things.  You can purchase items from the commodities market on any planet, and the credits will be deducted from your bank automatically.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 63, 'banker_bank_question_2', 'Can I store items in the bank?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 64, 'banker_bank_answer_2', 'Any items you store in this bank will be transferred to your new bank.  Once you get to your planet, join any bank there and we''ll send these items along.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 65, 'banker_bazaar_1', 'Once you''ve deposited your money at the bank terminal, browse the Item Dispenser to see if there is any equipment you''d like to purchase.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 66, 'banker_bazaar_reply_1', 'You didn''t give me very much money.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 67, 'banker_bazaar_2', 'I think The Empire is being more than generous.  Do you know how much it cost us to capture the transport you were on, kill the crew, search for secret cargo holds... not to mention pulling you out of the fire!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 68, 'banker_bazaar_reply_2', 'But that transport wasn''t smuggling anything!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 69, 'banker_bazaar_3', 'Ah, but now, how were we supposed to know that without capturing the transport first?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 70, 'trooper_move_along', 'Move along.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 71, 'leave_me_alone', 'Oh leave me alone!   I''ve lost everything!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 72, 'darn_empire', 'The empire has ruined us!  We had our life savings on that transport!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 73, 'ins_user_bark_1', 'There''s a crazy criminal on the loose!  I hope you''ve insured your items!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 74, 'ins_user_bark_2', 'All my items are insured... are yours?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 75, 'ins_user_bark_3', 'It''s a dangerous world.  I''m sure glad there''s an insurance terminal right here.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 76, 'greeter1_bark1', 'Ah, I see we have another refugee from the freighter.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 77, 'greeter1_bark2', 'Well, you''re one of the lucky ones.  Most passengers didn''t survive.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 78, 'greeter1_bark3', 'You should know better than to take passage with criminals.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 79, 'pirate_taunt2', 'You''ll never take me alive!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 80, 'pirate_taunt1', 'Come any closer and I''ll shoot!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 81, 'pirate_taunt3', 'Well I bet you weren''t expecting.... A GRENADE!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 82, 'pirate_taunt4', 'What the...?  This grenade is defective!  Oh no!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 83, 'pirate_attack', 'I''ll kill ya!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 84, 'convo_1_reply_3', 'The survivors?  You mean the Empire killed civilian passengers?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 85, 'convo_1_explain', 'They weren''t civilians.  They were dissidents.  Officially, anyway. Now, go get your free supplies from this drum right here, courtesy of the generosity of the Empire.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 86, 'off_1_greeting', 'Say... you''re still alive!  That''s amazing.');
INSERT INTO `client_strings` (`stringFile`, `index`, `name`, `value`) VALUES
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 87, 'off_1_start', 'Good show, in there.  You''re quite resourceful.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 88, 'off_1_reply_1', 'I''d be even better with a little training.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 89, 'off_1_reply_2', 'Combat isn''t really my thing.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 90, 'off_1_gotrain', 'Well there''s someone you should talk to right over there.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 91, 'off_1_gotrain2', 'Ha ha ha!  I suppose not.  Hey, there''s someone right here you should talk to about that.  I bet you could learn something.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 92, 'trainer_grunt', 'Huh?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 93, 'mission_hail', 'You there.  No time for that now.  I''ve got something for you to do.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 94, 'mission_1_start', 'What took you so long to get here?  The shuttle''s ready to leave!  Take these release documents to the Quartermaster and get yourself off my space station.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 95, 'mission_1_reply_1', 'Where is the Quartermaster?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 96, 'mission_1_reply_2', 'Will do!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 97, 'mission_1_waypoint', 'Here are your release documents.  Now get moving!  The Quartermaster is just down the hall, there.\n'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 98, 'quarter_greeting', 'Finally!  The last of the survivors, I take it?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 99, 'quarter_nodocs', 'You don''t have your release papers?  Well you''d better go get them from the Corporal.  Make it snappy!  Hup!  Hup!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 100, 'release_docs', 'Release Documents'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 101, 'quarter_1_start', 'Ah!  I see you have the proper documents there.  I''ll just take those from you.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 102, 'quarter_1_reply_1', 'Can I leave now?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 103, 'quarter_1_reply_2', 'Where are you sending me?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 104, 'quarter_1_go', 'You may use the travel terminal here and purchase a ticket to anywhere you want to go.  And don''t worry about the cost, the Empire will be picking up the tab on this one.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 105, 'quarter_wait', 'Wait a minute there!  You can''t use that travel terminal without the proper authorization.  Do you have your release documents on you?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 107, 'shout_panic1', 'Aaaaiiiiiii!  We''re all gonna die!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 108, 'shout_panic2', 'Mad pirate on the loose!  He''s got a bomb!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 109, 'shout_panic3', 'Someone DO something!!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 110, 'shout_panic4', 'Shouldn''t you be taking care of that crazy pirate or SOMETHING?!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 111, 'convo_4_start', 'Y-you can''t go IN there.  He cut them to pieces!  He''s crazy...!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 112, 'convo_4_reply_1', 'Calm down, I''m sure that everything will be under control soon.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 113, 'convo_4_reply_2', 'So how do I get out of here?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 114, 'convo_4_explain_1', 'Uh huh.  Look, y-you look pretty capable.  C-could you take a peek and see if there are any survivors in the hallway?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 115, 'convo_4_reply_3', 'Why don''t you go?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 116, 'convo_4_reply_4', 'Sure, I''ll check for survivors.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 117, 'convo_4_explain_2', 'The only way through is here.  Past... him.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 118, 'convo_4_reply_5', 'Then I guess I have to go that way.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 119, 'convo_4_reply_6', 'Sure, I''ll check for survivors.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 120, 'convo_4_explain_3', 'I, uh, need to stand guard.  In case reinforcements come.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 121, 'convo_4_weapon_1', 'Wait, you''ll need a weapon.  Uh, this is against regs, but... look, just don''t tell anyone.  Here.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 122, 'convo_4_reply_7', 'Thank you.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 123, 'convo_4_end', 'Sure, whatever.  Look, I think I''ll stand guard from the other side of the room, Ok?  And whatever you do, don''t get this maniac angry!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 124, 'convo_4_repeat', 'What are you doing here?  Get a move on.  I''m, uh, still guarding here.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 125, 'nervous_guy1', 'You couldn''t PAY me to go down that hallway!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 126, 'nervous_guy2', 'That pirate is crazy!  He blocked up the hallway and threatens anyone that goes near him!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 127, 'nervous_guy3', 'I bet the Empire will send him to the spice mines on Kessel'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 128, 'nervous_guy4', 'You can''t be thinking of going down that hallway?!  Didn''t you hear?  CRAZY PIRATE ON THE LOOSE!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 129, 'nervous_guy5', 'I wish I could go home...'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 130, 'celeb_guy1', 'I can''t believe that crazy pirate is dead.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 131, 'celeb_guy2', 'That must have been a tough battle.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 132, 'celeb_guy3', 'I''m sure glad that''s over with.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 133, 'celeb_guy4', 'Good thing someone came along to kill that pirate.  We''d have been trapped in here forever.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 134, 'celeb_guy5', 'I hate pirates.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 135, 'mission_repeat', 'Stop messing around with that terminal and deliver your papers to the Quartermaster!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 136, 'trapped_guy1', 'I don''t understand why you won''t give me release documents too...'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 137, 'trapped_guy2', 'I was going to kill that pirate.  It''s not my fault someone beat me to it.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 138, 'trapped_guy3', 'So I''ll be shipped off to the spice mines?  That''s not fair!  I heard someone killed the pirate and you''re letting them go!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 139, 'trapped_guy4', 'This is an outrage!  I demand my release papers this instant!  Uh... please?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 140, 'trapped_guy5', 'You destroyed my ship!  Ruined my life!  And now you''re refusing to release me!  Who is in charge here?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 141, 'good_job', 'Good job with that pirate, but what are you doing back here?  Go back through the big room where the pirate was.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 142, 'refugee1', 'They''re going to ship us off to the spice mines of Kessel.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 143, 'refugee2', 'The Emperor has disbanded the Senate, now the Empire can do whatever it wants.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 144, 'refugee3', 'But we''re innocent!  We weren''t carrying any contraband.  They attacked us for no reason.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 145, 'refugee4', 'I never should have left Alderaan... Oh, wait...'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 146, 'refugee5', 'I told you we couldn''t outrun an Imperial Star Destroyer.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_convo.stf', 147, 'quarter_1_go_nochoice', 'You may use the travel terminal here and be on your way.  And don''t worry about the cost of transportation, the Empire will be picking up the tab on this one.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 1, 'crafting_artisan_body', 'You''ve got the tools to survey for all the resources you need... except hides!  If you want to advance as an artisan, you''d better make some cash to trade for the hides you''ll need.  Then you can buy hides at the commodities market.  Maybe there are some missions you can do to earn some money.  Seek out a mission terminal and begin your career as a crafter.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 2, 'outdoors_scout_body', 'Well don''t stand around here reading the holonet all day long - get out there and Scout.  Artisans will need the hides that only you can provide, so remember to harvest resources from the creatures and bring their hides back to the commodities market.  You can even earn some money along the way by taking a mission.  Why don''t you stop by a mission terminal on your way out of town?'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 3, 'social_entertainer_body', 'After a hard day''s work everyone needs a chance to relax and unwind... and you''re just the person they need to see.  Your services will always be in demand at the local cantina, and if you don''t like working for tips then you could seek out a mission from the local mission board.  You might even find a mission custom-tailored for a person of your obvious talent!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 4, 'combat_marksman_body', 'Marksmen are always in demand.  Seek out a mission terminal or just ask around town to see if anyone has anything they need shot.  You''re just the person to do it!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 5, 'combat_brawler_body', 'A brawler like yourself can earn good money by doing missions for people.  Just ask around to see if anyone has anything they need you to do, or seek out a mission terminal.  Careful not to get in over your head though.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 6, 'science_medic_body', 'A good medic is hard to come by, so you''ll always be in demand.  You can heal people at the local hospital, and there are always plenty of wounded to tend to.  If you don''t feel comfortable charging for your services, maybe you should take a mission from the local mission terminal to earn some cash.   You''re going to need to buy supplies to heal people, after all.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 7, 'crafting_artisan_subject', 'You''re going to need some money!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 8, 'combat_brawler_subject', 'So you like to hit people'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 9, 'combat_marksman_subject', 'There''s no match for a good blaster'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 10, 'outdoors_scout_subject', 'Good scouts are hard to come by'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 11, 'science_medic_subject', 'There are injured people that need your attention!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 12, 'social_entertainer_subject', 'Local Cantina Seeks Entertainer'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 13, 'welcome_subject', 'Welcome to Star Wars Galaxies'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 15, 'welcome_body', 'You have taken your first steps into the immense universe of Star Wars. This game mail is meant to give you a quick welcome and overview. If you need additional details on anything about the game, don''t be afraid to bring up the Holocron (default: CTRL H). It offers easy-to-navigate chapters that not only teach you the game, but also gives you starting missions.\n\nUnlike many other games, there is no ''one'' way to play Star Wars Galaxies. You will be able to live in and interact with the Star Wars universe in a way you never have been able to before.\n\nIf you are looking for a little direction to get started, we recommend finding a local mission terminal to take some missions. After making some credits doing simple delivery or destroy missions, you may want to start upgrading your equipment. Eventually, you''ll want to converse with non-player characters to find more interesting and lucrative missions or you may want to head to the adventure Theme Parks like Jabba''s Palace on Tatooine.\n\nAfter that, you goals are largely determined by what you are interested in. For example, you may want to join the Rebellion or Empire and work your way up through the military ranks. You may wish to master multiple professions and become renown throughout the galaxy for your skills. You may want to acquire, make, or sell the best equipment in the galaxy. You might want to explore the ten worlds and find a perfect spot to build your home. You may even want to try to unlock the secret to opening a second character slot that is Force-sensitive (warning: this is extremely difficult, mysterious and dangerous). The choice is really up to you.\n \nYour best source for in-depth information on the game will come from other players. You can find players who are ready and willing to answer your questions right now by typing /who newbiehelper. Simply pick one off the list in your chat window and send your question by typing: /tell [player name] I''m new, could you please help me?\n\nAs a final note, the game is designed around the recommended default Star Wars Galaxies controls. However if you are more comfortable with a different control set up (EQ style, FPS style or Isometric style), you can quickly remap the entire keyboard layout in the Option menus (default CTRL ) - Controls tab - Keymap button - use the dropdown menu).\n\nOn behalf of the entire development team, thank you and enjoy your time in Star Wars Galaxies. May the Force be with you.\n'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 16, 'collector_subject', 'Collector''s Edition'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/newbie_mail.stf', 17, 'collector_body', 'You are using the Star Wars Galaxies Collector''s Edition.  This character has a special item which is only available to Collector''s Edition Users.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 1, 'welcome', 'Welcome to Star Wars Galaxies.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 2, 'movement_keyboard', 'Use the arrow keys to move.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 3, 'movement_mouse', 'Or hold down the right mouse-button to move forward.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 4, 'lookaround', 'You can look around by moving your mouse.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 5, 'mousewheel', 'Using the mouse-wheel, scroll forward to zoom into your character.  Notice that if you zoom in all the way, you''ll be in first-person mode.  Scroll backwards to zoom-out of your character, and into third-person mode.  You can also zoom your camera in and out by pressing the keypad plus and minus keys.  Try zooming between 1st and 3rd person.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 6, 'radar', 'If you''re going down that hallway, you might want advanced warning of what''s down there.  This is your radar.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 7, 'chatwindow', 'This is your chat window.  Type here to speak to your fellow players.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 8, 'chatprompt', 'Go ahead and try it.  Just type what you want to say and then press ENTER.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 9, 'repeatchatprompt', 'Don''t be shy.  Type something in your chatwindow and press Enter.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 10, 'move_to_item_room', 'Excellent!  Come through the door and down the hallway there.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 11, 'repeat_item_room_prompt', 'Come on.  Don''t keep me waiting all day.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 12, 'open_status_prompt', 'Good job.  Now I want you to look at your character status screen.  Press CTRL-C.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 13, 'close_status_prompt', 'Press CTRL-C again to toggle your character status screen off.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 14, 'prompt_open_box', 'To open the box just click and hold until you see the radial menu appear.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 15, 'prompt_choose_open', 'Great!  Now select the Open option to access the contents of the container.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 16, 'repeat_open_box', 'You might find something in the box you need.  Click and hold your mouse-button down on the box until you see the radial menu.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 17, 'open_me', '*Open Me!*\n'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 18, 'prompt_take_items', 'You can take these items by clicking-and-holding until you get the radial menu option on each item.  Pick up all of the items, and then click the X in the upper-right-hand corner of the container to close the box.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 19, 'prompt_select_pickup', 'Now choose the Pick Up option to move the item to your inventory.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 20, 'pickup_complete', 'You''ve put the item in your inventory.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 21, 'yoink', '*Yoink!*'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 22, 'visit_commerce_room', 'Proceed to the next room.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 23, 'repeat_visit_commerce', 'No need to stick around here all day.  Walk down the corridor to the next area.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 24, 'explain_freemouse', 'Notice that your mouse mode changed when you opened that container.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 25, 'explain_freemouse_toggle', 'You can toggle the mouse mode yourself with the ALT key.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 26, 'explain_inventory', 'You can examine your inventory by pressing CTRL-I.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 27, 'prompt_find_food', 'Scroll through your inventory until you locate one of the food items that you''ve just picked-up.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 28, 'prompt_use_item', 'Select the Use option to use this item.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 29, 'explain_item_used', 'You used the item on yourself.  Food will help increase your attributes.  Medicine will help you recover damage to your attributes.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 30, 'show_toolbar', 'This is your toolbar.  You can put things on it for instant access.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 31, 'move_to_toolbar', 'Move a food item from your inventory to a blank slot on your toolbar.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 32, 'use_toolbar', 'To use the item on your toolbar, press the function-key which corresponds with the toolbar slot.  F1 is the first slot.  F12 is the last slot.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 33, 'mousewheel_repeat', 'Give it a try.  Scroll out to 3rd-person and take a look at yourself.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 34, 'repeat_status_prompt', 'Press CTRL-C to view your character status screen.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 35, 'repeat_closestatus_prompt', 'Now press CTRL-C again to close your character status screen.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 36, 'repeat_open_inventory', 'Press CTRL-I to open your inventory, and select one of the food items you found in the crate.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 37, 'close_inventory', 'Press CTRL-I again to close your inventory window.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 38, 'explain_alt_key', 'Press the ALT key to toggle free-mouse mode on and off.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 39, 'bazaar_flytext', '*Shop!*'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 40, 'bank_flytext', '*Access the bank here!*'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 41, 'bank_info_1', 'Banks let you deposit and withdraw cash on hand.  You can also use the bank to store items.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 42, 'bank_info_2', 'You can only retrieve your items from the bank in which you stored the item.  You can only store items in the bank you''ve joined.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 43, 'bank_info_3', 'Although you can change banks at any time, you can only be a member of one bank at a time.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 44, 'bank_info_4', 'You can spend credits from your bank account at most terminals.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 45, 'bank_info_5', 'When you find hard credits (cash on hand), be sure to deposit them in your bank as soon as possible to avoid losing them.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 46, 'bazaar_info_1', 'This is an item dispenser.  You can use it to buy basic items in the game.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 47, 'bazaar_info_2', 'In addition to the basic item dispensers, you''ll find a number of terminals that will connect you to the galactic bazaar.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 48, 'bazaar_info_3', 'Everything from large quantities of resources, to specialized items can be bought and sold at the bazaar terminal.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 49, 'move_to_cloning', 'Take the elevator down and visit our state-of-the-art cloning facility.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 50, 'declare_cloned', 'Your clone data has been saved!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 51, 'declare_insured', 'All of your items have been insured!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 53, 'explain_combat_1', 'In combat, you can spend your HEALTH, MIND or ACTION pools to invoke special attacks.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 54, 'explain_combat_2', 'The ATTACK option on the radial menu will be the default attack for hostile creatures.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 55, 'explain_combat_3', 'You can attack hostile creatures simply by double-clicking them.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 56, 'menu_tatooine', 'Tatooine'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 57, 'menu_corellia', 'Corellia'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 58, 'menu_naboo', 'Naboo'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 59, 'menu_travel', 'DESTINATION'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 60, 'choose_destination', 'Please select a destination from the sub-menu.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 61, 'part_1', 'PART ONE OF NINE (movement and chat)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 62, 'part_2', 'PART TWO OF NINE (conversing with npcs and inventory)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 63, 'part_3', 'PART THREE OF NINE (banking and shopping)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 64, 'part_4', 'PART FOUR OF NINE (cloning and insurance)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 65, 'part_5', 'PART FIVE OF NINE (combat moves and radar)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 66, 'part_6', 'PART SIX OF NINE (combat)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 67, 'part_7', 'PART SEVEN OF NINE (skill training)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 68, 'part_8', 'PART EIGHT OF NINE (missions and waypoints)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 69, 'part_9', 'PART NINE OF NINE (bye!)'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 70, 'part_10', 'PART TEN OF ELEVEN'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 71, 'part_11', 'PART ELEVEN OF ELEVEN'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 72, 'radar_more', 'The red dots show potentially aggressive entities.  Yellow dots indicate peaceful life signatures.  You can also access an overlay map with CTRL-M.  Press CTRL-M again to turn it off.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 73, 'loot_pirate', 'Congratulations!  The pirate has been destroyed.  Now you can loot his corpse by clicking and holding your mouse on him until you get the radial menu option to LOOT.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 74, 'tut_08', 'Move forward and click-and-hold your mouse on the Imperial Officer until the radial menu appears.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 75, 'tut_09', 'He is now your look-at target.  His name appears over his head.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 76, 'tut_10', 'Click and hold the mouse button to get  a radial menu on the Imperial Officer.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 77, 'tut_11', 'Do you see the option to converse?  While holding your mouse button, move to the converse option and let go of the mouse button to select it.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 78, 'tut_12', 'Now you''re in a conversation.  You can choose one of the responses to the right with your mouse.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 79, 'tut_13', 'Remember, you don''t speak to other players this way.  Just type to talk to other players.  When you are finished conversing with the Imperial Officer, select the STOP CONVERSING option.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 80, 'tut_53', 'Mission terminals like those to your left are located throughout the world.  Whenever you want a quick adventure you can always take a job from a mission terminal.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 81, 'tut_54', 'You can also speak to npcs and do tasks for them.  There''s one over there who has something for you to do.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 82, 'tut_57', 'Converse with the Quartermaster.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 83, 'release_docs', 'Release Documents'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 84, 'oath_explain', 'You are required to promise to obey the code of conduct and to treat your fellow players with respect, before moving on.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 85, 'the_oath', 'I promise to treat my fellow players and citizens with respect and to obey the code of conduct'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 86, 'tut_60', 'Thank you.  You are now a citizen of Star Wars Galaxies.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 87, 'the_promise', 'I promise'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 88, 'tut_00_toolbardrag', 'You can drag items into your toolbar for easy access.  Simply click on the item and then drag it to an open slot on your toolbar.  Press the corresponding function key to use the item.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 89, 'receive_weapon', 'A weapon has been added to your inventory.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 90, 'clone_here', '*Clone!*'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 91, 'insure_here', '*Insurance!*'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 92, 'tut_44_attacking', 'When you hover your cursor over someone, your cursor changes to let you know that you can attack them.  Double-clicking them will attack them.  You can also cycle through targets with the tab key.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 93, 'mission_terminal', 'You cannot take a mission from this terminal.  To take a mission, you will need to find a mission terminal on a planet.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 94, 'tut_55_waypoints', 'Waypoints indicate destinations.  When you have a job or mission, you can follow the waypoint on your radar.  They appear light blue.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 95, 'make_promise', 'To swear your oath, please type the words I PROMISE into your chat window, and press ENTER.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 96, 'swear_reminder', 'You cannot become a citizen of Star Wars Galaxies until you promise to abide by the code of conduct.  To swear your oath, type I PROMISE into the chat window and hit the ENTER key.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 97, 'tut_45', 'The hallway is blocked by debris.  Attack it to destroy it.  Then proceed to the next room to face your enemy.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 98, 'tut_43', 'You can zoom the overlay map using the mousewheel, while holding down the CTRL key.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 99, 'tut_50', 'You''ve picked up your first skill.  There are many skills to master in your chosen profession and there are advanced professions that only open up once you have mastered many skills.  You can check your skills using the skills window.  You can reach this with the skills button on the button bar, or by pressing CTRL-S.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 100, 'tut_51', 'You can also check your character status after your fight, by pressing the character-sheet button on the button bar, or CTRL-C.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 101, 'keymap', 'Star Wars Galaxies contains a variety of different keyboard layouts as well as the ability to remap keys.  After you arrive at your starting planet, access the Options menu by hitting  CTRL-O, select the Controls option and then the Keymap option.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 102, 'newbie_mail', 'You''ve received a message.  Press the letter-icon on  your button bar to access your email!'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 103, 'imp_name', 'Imperial Officer'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 104, 'quarter_name', 'The Quartermaster'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 105, 'wrong_bank', 'You cannot use this bank terminal.  Use the bank terminal in the middle of the room.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 106, 'tut_36', 'Move down the ramp toward the cloning and insurance terminals.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 107, 'tut_56', 'Move to the next room to deliver your release documents to the Quartermaster.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 108, 'select_dest', 'Select your destination by clicking on one of the planets on the screen.  When you have selected the planet, select which city you wish to travel to by clicking on the picture to the right of the screen.  When you are ready to travel to the city, click on the arrow in the lower right-hand corner of the screen.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 109, 'tut_32', 'Banks let you deposit and withdraw cash on hand.  You can also use the bank to store items.  You can only retrieve your items from the bank in which you stored the item.  You can only store items in the bank you''ve joined.  Although you can change banks at any time, you can only be a member of one bank at a time.  You can spend credits from your bank account at most terminals.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 110, 'tut_33', 'When you find hard credits (cash on hand) be sure to deposit them in your bank as soon as possible to avoid losing them.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 111, 'tut_37', 'Use the cloning terminal.  You can do this through the radial menu, or you can just double-click.  The cursor changes when over a usable item.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 112, 'tut_38', 'Use the insurance terminal.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 113, 'tut_40', 'Converse with the soldier.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 114, 'tut_49', 'The Imperial Officer has directed you to a Skill Trainer.  Converse with the Skill Trainer to learn your first skill.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 115, 'holocube', 'This is your Holocron.  You can access it by pressing CTRL-H.  Whenever you need information about something in Star Wars Galaxies, press CTRL-H to find it in your Holocron.  To close this screen, press CTRL-H again.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 116, 'start_loc', 'Starting Location'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 117, 'stat_migration', 'Although your stats have been optimized for your starting profession, you may wish to change your stats in order to pursue a different profession, either instead of or in addition to your starting profession.  Once you are in the world, stat migration is a slow process:  Gradually moving points from one stat to another.  However, in this Planet Selection Room, you may migrate your stats and the changes will take effect immediately.  If you would like to change your stats now, press CTRL-C and choose the Stat Migration button.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 118, 'stat_open', 'Although your stats have been optimized for your starting profession, you may wish to change your stats in order to pursue a different profession, either instead of or in addition to your starting profession.  Once you are in the world, stat migration is a slow progress:  Gradually moving points from one stat to another.  However, in this Tutorial, you may migrate your stats and the changes will take effect immediately.'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 119, 'tut_28', 'Converse with the Imperial Officer'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 120, 'droid_name', 'Q-3PO'),
('string/en/newbie_tutorial/system_messages.stf', 121, 'waypoint', 'Waypoint'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 2, 'help_please_button', 'Help'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 3, 'no_help_needed_button', 'No'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 4, 'droid_greeting_begin_01', '[beep... clik... zwing... bweep... beep] \nGreetings, '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 5, 'yes_please_button', 'Yes'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 6, 'not_now_button', 'Not Now'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 7, 'brawler_added', '[beep... freetle... boop... whir] \nYou have joined the Brawler profession. I have downloaded some Brawler tasks so that you may learn more about being a Brawler.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 8, 'marksman_added', '[boop... boop... beep] \nYou have joined the Marksman profession. I have downloaded some Marksman tasks so that you may learn more about being a Marksman.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 9, 'medic_added', '[boop... clik... zweet] \nYou have joined the Medic profession. I have downloaded some Medic tasks so that you may learn more about being a Medic.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 10, 'scout_added', '[bwat... zzt... bweep... clik] \nYou have joined the Scout profession. I have downloaded some Scout tasks so that you may learn more about being a Scout.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 11, 'artisan_added', '[beep... boop... whir] \nYou have joined the Artisan profession. I have downloaded some Artisan tasks so that you may learn more about being an Artisan.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 12, 'entertainer_added', '[beep... beep... bop] \nYou have joined the Entertainer profession. I have downloaded some Entertainment tasks so that you may learn more about being an Entertainer.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 13, 'general_greeting_prose_01', '[beep... clik] Greetings %TO.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 14, 'brawler_quest_01', '[beep... blip... zeek... boweep... clik] \nAs one who has chosen the Brawler approach to combat, you may wish to choose a style of melee fighting that suits you. The four primary approaches to melee combat are unarmed, the use of one-handed weapons, the use of two-handed weapons, and the use of polearm weapons. \n\nUnarmed combat, of course, doesn''t involve using a weapon. Basic weapons for the others are a survival knife (a one-handed weapon), a heavy axe (a two-handed weapon), and a wood staff (a polearm weapon). Which weapon would you like to use?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 15, 'brawler_quest_02', '[zwing... bleep... vwoot... whir] \nThe primary aim of a Brawler is victory in combat, and it''s time to begin working toward that. \n\nYour first task is to go to kill a creature. You''ll find some on the outskirts of this city. Kill any one creature you find to complete this task.\n\nBe sure to equip your weapon in order to use it in combat... unless, of course, you wish to fight unarmed. To equip a weapon, simply double-click it in your inventory. You can also use the radial menu on the weapon and choose "Equip".'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 16, 'brawler_quest_03', '[dadeep... blip... boop... boop] \nYou have special abilities that can aid you while fighting. The Berserk ability increases the damage you do in combat though you become a bit easier for your opponent to hit. \n\nUse Berserk while fighting and killing a creature.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 17, 'brawler_quest_04', '[bweep... tweet... bweeo... zzt] \nUsing a Lunge can extend your range a small amount, but more importantly it can change the posture of your target. This can render them helpless and often unable to attack until they recover. \n\nUse Lunge while fighting and killing a creature.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 18, 'brawler_quest_05', '[vwoot... beep... blip... boop]\nUsing Center of Being can provide you a defensive bonus by helping you avoid being hit by your opponent. \n\nUse Center of Being while fighting and killing a creature.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 19, 'brawler_quest_weapon_choice', '[beep... blip... zeek... boweep... clik] \nAs one who has chosen the Brawler approach to combat, you may wish to choose a style of melee fighting that suits you. The four primary approaches to melee combat are unarmed, the use of one-handed weapons, the use of two-handed weapons, and the use of polearm weapons. \n\nUnarmed combat, of course, doesn''t involve using a weapon. Basic weapons for the others are a survival knife (a one-handed weapon), a heavy axe (a two-handed weapon), and a wood staff (a polearm weapon). Which weapon would you like to use?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 20, 'marksman_quest_01', '[beep... whir... tweetle... clik] \nAs one who has chosen the Marksman approach to combat, you may wish to choose a style of ranged battle that suits you. There are close-range pistols, medium-range carbines, and long-range rifles.  \n\nThe basic weapons for each style are a CDEF pistol (a close-range weapon), a CDEF carbine (a medium-range weapon), and a CDEF rifle (a long-range weapon). Which weapon would you like to use?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 21, 'marksman_quest_02', '[boop... blip... zeet] \nThe primary aim of a Marksman is to defeat an opponent from a distance. It''s time to begin learning to do that. \n\nYour first task is to fight and kill a creature. You''ll find some on the outskirts of this city. Kill any one creature you find and this task will be complete.\n\nBe sure to equip your weapon in order to use it in combat. To equip a weapon, simply double-click it in your inventory. You can also use the radial menu on the weapon and choose "Equip".'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 22, 'marksman_quest_03', '[zwing... vwoot... razzle... beep]\nIf an enemy gets too near to you during combat, you may use Point Blank Single to fight them at close range. \n\nUse Point Blank Single while fighting and killing a creature.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 23, 'marksman_quest_04', '[bweep... bwat... tweetle]\n You have some special techniques that can aid you when in combat. The Overcharge Shot allows you to increase the amount of damage you can do, but also damages your weapon more than during normal use. \n\nUse Overcharge Shot while fighting and killing a creature.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 24, 'marksman_quest_weapon_choice', '[beep... whir... tweetle... clik] \nAs one who has chosen the Marksman approach to combat, you may wish to choose a style of ranged battle that suits you. There are close-range pistols, medium-range carbines, and long-range rifles. \n\nThe basic weapons for each style are a CDEF pistol (a close-range weapon), a CDEF carbine (a medium-range weapon), and a CDEF rifle (a long-range weapon). Which weapon would you like to use?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 25, 'scout_quest_01', '[bweep... whir... boop... zeet] \nBefore getting started, I must pass along some standard advice for one starting in the Scout profession. \n\nMost Scouts also take a combat profession such as Brawler or Marksman to aid them in the dangerous wilds. Especially when wishing to harvest resources.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 26, 'scout_quest_02', '[beep... whir... bwip... tweetle] \nScouts are experts at making good use of natural resources. While hunting, a Scout can harvest hides, meat, or bone from the creatures they kill. \n\nKill a creature and harvest resources from it. You''ll find suitable targets on the outskirts of town.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 27, 'scout_quest_03', '[clik... vwoot... freetle] \nThe resources harvested by a Scout can be used to craft various supplies the Scout can use. \n\nHunt enough creatures to gather at least 3 units of hides and 3 units of bone.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 28, 'scout_quest_04', '[beep... bwat... zzt... whir] \nUsing the hides and bones you harvested, craft some Lecepanine Dart traps. These can be used on creatures to aid you during combat.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 29, 'scout_quest_05', '[boop... blip... whir... zwing] \nScouts are also adept at erecting temporary camps that can have a variety of uses. \n\nUse a basic camp kit to place a camp in the wild. Gather resources and craft a basic camp kit if you no longer have one.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 30, 'scout_quest_recommendation', '[bweep... whir... boop... zeet] \nBefore getting started, I must pass along some standard advice for one starting in the scouting profession. \n\nMost Scouts also take a combat profession such as Brawler or Marksman to aid them in the dangerous wilds. Especially when wishing to harvest resources.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 31, 'entertainer_quest_01', '[whir... bleep... vwoot] \nDancing is one of the basic forms of entertainment that you can master as an Entertainer. \n\nPlease perform any dance.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 32, 'entertainer_quest_02', '[bwoop... tweet... razzle] \nAnother standard form of entertainment at your disposal is the performance of music. \n\nPlease play any piece of music.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 33, 'entertainer_quest_03_human', '[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] \nSome entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. \n\nYou next task is to use your image design skills and change your hair to a different style.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 34, 'entertainer_quest_04', '[beep... dadeet... blip] \nTo enhance your music or dancing, you will need to add flourishes while you perform. This will not only enhance your performance, but it also increases your effectiveness with various entertainer abilities.\n\nPlease play a song or dance a dance and add flourishes during your performance.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 35, 'entertainer_quest_05', '[bweet... whir... zeet] \nAn Entertainer can relieve Battle Fatigue for other players by performing music or dancing for them. They can only do this in a cantina or in a theater.\n\nFind a cantina or theater and go inside.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 36, 'entertainer_quest_06', '[clik... beep... zwing... beep] \nI have received a request from a local sociologist. She wishes to study the reaction of people to the latest trends in dance and music. \n\nAsk another player to either watch you dance or listen to you play music. Do this for a total of 7 players. You may perform for all 7 players at once or each of them individually, but you must entertain all 7 of them using the same type of performance... meaning dance for them or play music, but not both.\n\n'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 37, 'artisan_quest_01', '[tweet... boop... blip] \nAs an Artisan, you will need various resources to craft your goods. As someone new to the profession, your best method for finding these resources will be to survey for them. \n\nYour first task is to survey for any type of mineral.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 38, 'artisan_quest_02', '[bweepo...zeek... beep] \nNow that you have found some minerals in the area, take some resource samples. Continue until you have 8 units of a single type of mineral.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 39, 'artisan_quest_03', '[zzt... bweeo... boop...razzle] \nFor your next task, survey for and sample a metal. Any type will do, but you must find 19 units of the same type of metal to complete this task in addition to the 8 units of minerals you collected previously.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 40, 'artisan_quest_04', '[blip... bweep... dadeep] \nNow you have the resources required to craft a chemical survey device. Make one of them.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 41, 'artisan_quest_05', '[boop... clik... bweep... bzzt] \nI have downloaded a service contract that you should now be able to fulfill. A guild of hunters wishes to present a demonstration on basic rifle craftsmanship. The contract asks that you craft some rifles, and I''ll record your actions. The guild leaders will then edit together a holovid for their presentation.\n\nUse the Artisan knowledge you have gained to gather resources for 5 CDEF rifles and craft them. If you wish, you may craft these in practice mode so that you do not clutter your inventory with surplus rifles.\n\n'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 42, 'medic_quest_01', '[blip... whir... beep] \nBefore getting started, I must pass along some standard advice for one starting in the medical profession.\n\nIf you wish to pursue the crafting of medical supplies, it is recommended that you consider also taking the Artisan profession so that you may survey for and sample resources.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 43, 'medic_quest_02', '[clik... boop... beep... bwoop] \nA majority of the medical practice takes place in a medical center, and most major cities will have at least one medical center. You may also practice the healing arts while in a camp or in the presence of a droid that has a medical module.\n\nYour next task is to find and enter a medical center.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 44, 'medic_quest_03', '[buweep... zeet... razzle] \nTo better serve those who seek your medical expertise, it is best to know what ails them. \n\nDiagnose another player to determine what wounds they have.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 45, 'medic_quest_04', '[beep... zzt... tweet] \nThe basis of the medical profession is healing wounds. Healing wounds requires medical supplies, but you may tend wounds without needing anything but your willpower. \n\nTend wounds on any one player. You must be in a medical center to do this.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 46, 'delayed_accepting_quest', '[boop...bleep..bleep... whir... clik] \nVery well. When you are ready to begin, simply use my radial menu. When you click on me and the radial menu appears, hover over the menu option labeled "Profession Quests" and then choose the submenu for the profession about which you are ready to learn.  And remember that I am authorized to reward you for your progress as you complete these tasks.\n\nIf I''m ever needed but not out by your side, you may call me from my control device in your datapad. Simply open your datapad (CTRL-D) and then select the control device with my name. It will be in the "Data" tab in your datapad. Click on my control device and use the radial menu choice to "Call" me.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 47, 'give_quest_button', 'Quest'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 48, 'thank_you_button', 'Close'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 49, 'menu_quests', 'Profession Quests'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 50, 'submenu_brawler', 'Brawler'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 51, 'submenu_marksman', 'Marksman'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 52, 'submenu_scout', 'Scout'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 53, 'submenu_artisan', 'Artisan'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 54, 'submenu_entertainer', 'Entertainer'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 55, 'submenu_medic', 'Medic'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 56, 'brawler_quest_06', '[beep... whir... tweetle... whir... clik]\nI have downloaded a job with a more substantial payment. \n\nA local scholar would like to study the stresses of combat on one such as yourself who is still new to the art of melee battle. He requires that you find and kill 10 creatures. I shall record your actions and transmit the recordings to him when you''ve completed this task.\n\n'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 57, 'marksman_quest_05', '[bweep... tweet... boop... zwing] \nA nice job offer has just been downloaded to me. A local merchant wants some nice action pictures to use in advertisements for his weapons. \n\nFind and kill 10 creatures, and I will transmit images of your combat to him to fulfill the contract.\n\n'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 58, 'scout_quest_06', '[beep... blip... whir... vweet... clik] \nI have accepted a contract on your behalf. An enterprising local merchant wishes to show that environment and climate can cause fluctuations in the quality of hides harvested from creatures in an area. He will require a small sample from each of the hides you gather, and he will then study them to put together a set of data for his research.\n\nHarvest hides from creatures until the total amount of hides you''ve harvested equals 90 or more. I''ll take a small research sample from each hide and pass those samples on to the merchant.\n\n'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 59, 'heavy_axe_button', 'Axe'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 60, 'survival_knife_button', 'Knife'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 61, 'wooden_staff_button', 'Staff'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 62, 'cdef_pistol_button', 'Pistol');
INSERT INTO `client_strings` (`stringFile`, `index`, `name`, `value`) VALUES
('string/en/new_player.stf', 63, 'cdef_rifle_button', 'Rifle'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 64, 'cdef_carbine_button', 'Carbine'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 65, 'continue_button', 'Continue'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 66, 'credits_reward', '%DI credits have been deposited into your bank account.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 67, 'medic_quest_05', '[blip... whir... bweep] \nCrafting stimpacks allows you to better heal damage taken in combat, just as crafting medpacks will allow you to better heal wounds.\n\nI''ve placed resources for one stimpack into your inventory. Please use them to craft a stimpack.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 68, 'medic_quest_06', '[beep... bloot... vweet... clik] \nA local doctor is gathering data on the effectiveness of tending wounds without the use of medicines. She intends to chart the results of these techniques and study the toll taken on Medics who use them.\n\nTend wounds on 5 different players, and I will send her the data she desires.\n\n'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 69, 'okay_button', 'Okay'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 70, 'brawler_quest_complete', '[beep... whir... clik... tweetle... bweep] \nCongratulations on finishing the tasks for the Brawler profession. \n\nContinue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.\n\nIf you''d like to try any of the other starting professions (Marksman, Scout, Medic, Artisan, or Entertainer), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don''t worry... I can help you with those professions as well.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 71, 'marksman_quest_complete', '[beep... boop... clik... tweetle... bweep] \nCongratulations on finishing the tasks for the Marksman profession. \n\nContinue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.\n\nIf you''d like to try any of the other starting professions (Brawler, Scout, Medic, Artisan, or Entertainer), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don''t worry... I can help you with those professions as well.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 72, 'scout_quest_complete', '[bweep... zeet... tweetle... boop... bweep] \nCongratulations on finishing the tasks for the Scout profession. \n\nContinue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.\n\nIf you''d like to try any of the other starting professions (Brawler, Marksman, Medic, Artisan, or Entertainer), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don''t worry... I can help you with those professions as well.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 73, 'entertainer_quest_complete', '[beep... zwing... tweet... bweep... beep] \nCongratulations on finishing the tasks for the Entertainer profession. \n\nContinue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.\n\nIf you''d like to try any of the other starting professions (Brawler, Marksman, Scout, Medic, or Artisan), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don''t worry... I can help you with those professions as well.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 74, 'artisan_quest_complete', '[beep... clik... beep... whir... blip] \nCongratulations on finishing the tasks for the Artisan profession. \n\nContinue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.\n\nIf you''d like to try any of the other starting professions (Brawler, Marksman, Scout, Medic, or Entertainer), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don''t worry... I can help you with those professions as well.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 75, 'medic_quest_complete', '[zwing... razzle... zwing... beep... whir] \nCongratulations on finishing the tasks for the Medic profession. \n\nContinue using what you have learned to progress in this profession. Well done and happy journeys.\n\nIf you''d like to try any of the other starting professions (Brawler, Marksman, Scout, Artisan, or Entertainer), simply speak to a trainer for the profession you wish to try and tell them you are interested in learning that profession. And don''t worry... I can help you with those professions as well.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 76, 'new_player_vehicle_coupon', 'A Vehicle Rental Device'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 77, 'new_player_vehicle_coupon_d', 'Using this device will upload a rental vehicle device to your datapad.\n\nWhen you first use this vehicle rental device, a vehicle control device will be placed in your datapad, and your rental vehicle will be called for the first time for you to ride. Thereafter to call your rental vehicle, use the vehicle control device in your datapad (CTRL-D).\n\nYour rental vehicle can be called 5 times before the rental contract expires. Once the vehicle is called, you may ride it at will until it is stored again. Remember that when you first use this device, your rental vehicle is called for the first time which will then leave you with 4 more opportunities to call and use it.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 78, 'new_player_cloning_coupon', 'A Cloning Facility Authorization Release'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 79, 'new_player_cloning_coupon_d', 'This cloning facility authorization release can be used to store your clone data at a cloning facility at no cost. It may only be used once.\n\nWhen you use a cloning terminal to store your clone data at a cloning facility, you will be given the option of using this authorization release instead of paying the fee.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 80, 'new_player_travel_coupon_d', 'This travel voucher can be used to purchase a shuttleport or starport ticket at no cost. It may only be used once.\n\nWhen you use a travel terminal to purchase a travel ticket, you will be given the option of using this travel voucher to pay for the ticket.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 81, 'new_player_travel_coupon', 'A Travel Voucher'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 82, 'refused_quest_help', '[bweep...bleep..blip... zonk... tweet] \nVery well. If you need help, simply use my radial menu. When you click on me and the radial menu appears, hover over the menu option labeled "Profession Quests" and then choose the submenu for the profession about which you are ready to learn.  And remember that I am authorized to reward you for your progress as you complete these tasks.\n\nIf I''m ever needed but not out by your side, you may call me from my control device in your datapad. Simply open your datapad (CTRL-D) and then select the control device with my name. It will be in the "Data" tab in your datapad. Click on my control device and use the radial menu choice to "Call" me.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 83, 'lets_start_button', 'Start'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 84, 'help_now_button', 'Help'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 85, 'entertainer_quest_03_twilek', '[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] \nSome entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. \n\nYou next task is to use your image design skills and change your lekku to a different style.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 86, 'entertainer_quest_03_trandoshan', '[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] \nSome entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. \n\nYou next task is to use your image design skills and change your skull ridges to a different style.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 87, 'entertainer_quest_03_zabrak', '[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] \nSome entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. \n\nYou next task is to use your image design skills and change your horn pattern to a different style.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 88, 'entertainer_quest_03_moncalamari', '[beep... clik... tweetle... clik... whir... zang] \nYour next task was to restyle your hair, but as a Mon Calamari, you do not have hair or anything else to style. I have been authorized to skip this step and move on to the next one.\n\nBefore I do, I''d like to make sure you know that you can help others style their hair by grouping with them, then targeting them, and then either selecting the Image Design radial menu option or typing /imagedesign. If you progress as an Image Designer, you will eventually learn how to change the style and color your skull markings... among other things.\n\nLet''s move on.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 89, 'given_survey_device', 'A mineral survey device has been added to your inventory.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 90, 'given_crafting_tool', 'A generic crafting tool has been added to your inventory.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 91, 'given_slitherhorn', 'A slitherhorn has been added to your inventory.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 92, 'default_cancel_button', 'Cancel'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 93, 'default_okay_button', 'Okay'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 94, 'default_revert_button', 'Revert'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 95, 'default_text', 'Warning... I have nothing to say.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 96, 'entertainer_quest_03_wookiee', '[beep... clik... tweetle... clik... whir... zang] \nYour next task was intended to be to restyle your hair, but as a Wookiee, your fur cannot be styled so easily. I have been authorized to skip this step and move on to the next one.\n\nBefore I do, I''d like to make sure you know that you can help others style their hair by grouping with them, then targeting them, and then either selecting the Image Design radial menu or typing /imagedesign. If you progress as an Image Designer, you will eventually learn how to change your fur color and markings... among other things.\n\nLet''s move on.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 97, 'entertainer_quest_03_rodian', '[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] \nSome entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. \n\nYou next task is to use your image design skills and change your frills to a different style.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 98, 'entertainer_quest_03_bothan', '[boop... zeet... zwing... clik] \nSome entertainers choose to follow the path of becoming an Image Designer. Image design can involve many things such as hair styling, body sculpting, and even skin tinting. \n\nYou next task is to use your image design skills and change your hair to a different style.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 101, 'given_cloning_coupon', 'A cloning facility authorization release has been placed in your inventory. Examine it for more details.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 102, 'given_travel_coupon', 'A travel voucher has been placed in your inventory. Examine it for more details.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 103, 'given_vehicle_coupon', 'A vehicle rental device has been placed in your inventory. Examine it for more details.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 104, 'artisan_quest_00', '[beep... tweet... whir] \nAre you ready to learn more about the Artisan profession? I''ve downloaded some Artisan tasks that will help.\n\nReady to begin?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 105, 'brawler_quest_00', '[beep... clik... boop... whir] \nAre you ready to learn more about the Brawler profession? I''ve downloaded some Brawler tasks that will help.\n\nReady to begin?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 106, 'entertainer_quest_00', '[beep... beep... bop] \nAre you ready to learn more about the Entertainer profession? I''ve downloaded some Entertainer tasks that will help.\n\nReady to begin?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 107, 'scout_quest_00', '[bwat... zzt... bweep... whir] \nAre you ready to learn more about the Scout profession? I''ve downloaded some Scout tasks that will help.\n\nReady to begin?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 108, 'marksman_quest_00', '[boop... beep... beep] \nAre you ready to learn more about the Marksman profession? I''ve downloaded some Marksman tasks that will help.\n\nReady to begin?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 109, 'medic_quest_00', '[boop... zweet... whir] \nAre you ready to learn more about the Medic profession? I''ve downloaded some Medic tasks that will help.\n\nReady to begin?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 110, 'profession_quest_menus', 'Select the submenu under Profession Quests for the profession in which you are interested.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 111, 'task_complete_reward_01', '%TU tells you "[bleep... whir... zing... boop... razz] Well done in completing your %TT task. You have been granted bonus Experience Points and a reward of %DI credits."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 112, 'task_complete_no_reward_01', '%TU tells you "[bleep... whir... boop] Well done in completing your %TT task."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 113, 'task_complete_reward_02', '%TU tells you "[bwoop... whir... zing... boop... razz] Excellent job in completing your %TT task. You have been granted bonus Experience Points and a reward of %DI credits."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 114, 'task_complete_reward_03', '%TU tells you "[whir... zing... boop... bleep... razz] Your %TT task is complete. Very good. You have been granted bonus Experience Points and a reward of %DI credits."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 115, 'task_complete_reward_04', '%TU tells you "[whir... zing... boop... razz... whir] You have completed your %TT task and have been granted bonus Experience Points plus a reward of %DI credits."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 116, 'task_complete_reward_05', '%TU tells you "[whir... bleep... zing... boop... razz] You have done well and completed your %TT task. You have been granted bonus Experience Points and a reward of %DI credits."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 117, 'task_complete_no_reward_02', '%TU tells you "[bwoop... whir... boop] Excellent job in completing your %TT task."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 118, 'task_complete_no_reward_03', '%TU tells you "[whir... boop... bleep] Your %TT task is complete. Very good."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 119, 'task_complete_no_reward_04', '%TU tells you "[whir... boop... whir] You have completed your %TT task."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 120, 'task_complete_no_reward_05', '%TU tells you "[whir... bleep... boop] You have done well and completed your %TT task."'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 121, 'general_greeting_prose_02', '[bwoop... clik] Hello %TO.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 122, 'general_greeting_prose_03', '[tweet... clik] Salutations %TO.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 125, 'droid_greeting_end', 'I am your helper droid and will be helping you to learn more about any of the Starting Professions you wish to undertake.\n\nI have downloaded some tasks to help you get started. Would you like to begin?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 126, 'droid_greeting_begin_02', '[bwoop... clik... zwing... bweep... beep] \nHello, '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 127, 'droid_greeting_begin_03', '[tweet... clik... zwing... bweep... beep] \nSalutations, '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 128, 'general_combat_button', 'Combat'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 129, 'brawler_berserk', '[whir... clik... beep... tweetle... razz]\nWhile Berserk, you cause more melee damage to your targets but get hit more often in return.\n\nTo go Berserk, type "/berserk1" or you may drag Berserk 1 from the "Other" tab of your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 130, 'brawler_lunge', '[whir... clik... bweep... freet... blip]\nA Lunge attack can slightly extend your range, and has a chance to lower the posture of your target... possibly limiting their ability to attack or defend.\n\nTo use Lunge, you will need to type the command that goes with your style of attack: \n    For one-handed weapons, type /melee1hlunge1 <target>\n    For two-handed weapons, type /melee2hlunge1 <target>\n    For polearm weapons, type /polearmlunge1 <target>\n    For unarmed, type /unarmedlunge1 <target>\n\nIf you have your target selected, you can leave off the <target> part of the command.\n\nOr you may drag the appropriate Lunge 1 command from the "Combat" tab of your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 131, 'brawler_center_of_being', '[whir... clik... bleet... zzt... tweet]\nWhen using Center of Being, your character will focus on avoiding combat blows.\n\nTo use Center of Being, type "/centerofbeing" or you may drag Center of Being from the "Other" tab in your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 132, 'marksman_point_blank_single', '[whir... clik... vwoot... bwat... beep]\nA Point Blank Single attack can be performed at point blank range on a single target without suffering a penalty to hit.\n\nTo use a Point Blank Single attack, type "/pointblanksingle1 <target>" or you can select your target and then just type "/pointblanksingle1".\n\nAnother option is to drag Point Blank Single 1 from the "Combat" tab of your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 133, 'marksman_overcharge_shot', '[whir... clik... boop... dadeep... zeep]\nAn Overcharge Shot causes more damage to a target at the expense of your weapon''s power supply.\n\nTo use an Overcharge Shot, type "/overchargeshot1 <target>" or you may select your target and then just type "/overchargeshot1".\n\nAnother option is to drag Overcharge Shot 1 from the "Combat" tab of your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 134, 'entertainer_image_design', '[whir... clik... beep... boop... zweep]\nUsing Image Design allows you to alter the way your character looks, or to alter the way other characters look as long as they are in a group with you and consent to your changes.\n\nTo Image Design, type "/imagedesign <target''s name>". You may also simply click on your target to select them and then type "/imagedesign". If you aren''t targeting anyone, then you will image design yourself.\n\nAnother way to begin image designing is use the "Image Design" radial menu choice on a player with whom you are grouped.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 135, 'medic_diagnose', '[whir... clik... weet... blip... tweet]\nUsing Diagnose allows you to see what wounds your patient might have.\n\nTo use Diagnose, type "/diagnose <target''s name>". You may also click on your target to select them and then type "/diagnose".\n\nAnother option is to drag Diagnose from the "Other" tab of your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 136, 'medic_tend_wounds', '[whir... clik... bweep... bloop... zweet]\nUsing Tend Wounds heals the wounds of a specified physical attribute without the need for medicine.  Using this causes minor wounding to your focus and willpower.\n\nTo Tend Wounds, type "/tendwound <target''s name> <attribute>". You may also click on your target to select them and then type "/tendwound <attribute>".\n\nA third option is to drag Tend Wound from the "Other" tab of your Command Browser (CTRL-A) to your hotkey bar at the top of your screen and use the corresponding hotkey or click on it directly.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 137, 'general_entertainer_button', 'Entertainer Info'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 138, 'general_medic_button', 'Healing Info'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 139, 'calling_stored_helper_droid', '[zwoop... blip... clik... bweep]\nWhen I have been stored, you may call me from my control device in your datapad. \n\nSimply open your datapad (CTRL-D) and then select the control device with my name. It will be in the "Data" tab in your datapad. Click on my control device and use the radial menu choice to "Call" me.\n\nIf I''m currently in the world somewhere, instead of a "Call" menu option, you will see a "Store" menu option. You can use this choice to store me in my control device.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 140, 'vehicle_coupon_menu_call', 'Call Rental Vehicle'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 141, 'vehicle_coupon_is_not_owner', 'You are not authorized to use this rental device.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 142, 'vehicle_coupon_no_owner', 'This is an invaild rental device.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 143, 'given_fireworks', 'A firework device has been placed in your inventory.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 144, 'travel_coupon', 'Using A Travel Voucher'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 145, 'travel_coupon_use_text_option', 'Would you like to:\n\n- Use your Travel Voucher to purchase this ticket?\n- Or pay the fee to purchase this ticket?\n\nTicket Price: '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 146, 'travel_coupon_use_coupon_button', 'Use Voucher'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 147, 'travel_coupon_pay_credits_button', 'Pay Fee'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 149, 'travel_coupon_invaild', 'Warning: Travel Voucher is invalid. Aborting travel ticket purchase...'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 150, 'travel_coupon_use_text_no_money', 'Would you like to use your Travel Voucher to purchase this ticket?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 151, 'travel_coupon_cancelled', 'Ticket purchase cancelled.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 152, 'travel_coupon_cancel_button', 'Cancel'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 154, 'listbox_no_selection', 'Please select one of the professions in the list before clicking on "Okay".'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 155, 'droid_prompt_end', 'and welcome back. I am, as always, at your service.\n\nIf I may be of assistance, simply select the profession you want and then click on the "Okay" button.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 156, 'inventory_full', '[beep... zip... bwoop... clik]\nYou have no space in your inventory. Please make some room and then use my radial menu to try again when you are ready.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 157, 'completed_first_task', 'Congratulations on completing your first ever task! If you wish to celebrate, you can use these fireworks.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 158, 'completed_second_task', 'Whoo, you''re on  roll! Here''s an authorization release for any cloning facility... it lets you bind once for free. Enjoy!'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 159, 'completed_first_profession', 'Well done! You''ve completed an entire profession''s set of tasks. As a reward, take this vehicle rental. Have fun!'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 160, 'completed_third_task', 'You''re doing great! Here''s a travel voucher. Use it to get a free shuttleport or spaceport ticket! Wow!'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 161, 'entertainer_quest_06_b', 'Players Entertained: '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 162, 'artisan_quest_05_b', 'Rifles Crafted: '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 163, 'brawler_quest_06_b', 'Creatures Killed: '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 164, 'marksman_quest_05_b', 'Creatures Killed: '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 165, 'medic_quest_06_b', 'Players Healed: '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 166, 'scout_quest_06_b', 'Samples of Hide Harvested: '),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 167, 'submenu_cloning', 'Cloning'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 168, 'submenu_travel', 'Traveling'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 169, 'submenu_vehicle', 'Vehicle Use'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 170, 'menu_other', 'General Help'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 171, 'droid_periodic_check_end', 'I am merely checking to see if you might be in need of assistance.\n\nIf so, you need simply select the profession with which you would like help and then click on the "Okay" button.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 172, 'counter_not_update', '\n\n         (Please note that as you progress in this task,\n         the counter will not update without being re-opened.)'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 173, 'space_greeting', 'I am your helper droid, and I can help answer some questions you might have about becoming a pilot of a starship.\n\nPlease choose any topic shown below, and I will provide more information about it.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 174, 'space_option_how_to_find_ship', 'How do I get trained as a starship pilot?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 175, 'space_option_how_to_check_email', 'How do I check my email?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 176, 'space_option_how_to_travel', 'How do I travel to other ground locations?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 177, 'space_option_how_to_make_money', 'How do I make money?'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 178, 'space_info_how_to_find_ship', '[beep... bleep... freet... click]\nYour best bet to get a starship with which to start, as well as the training to fly one, would be to join an organization that will supply you with one. Such an organization might be part of the military, as with the Imperial Navy or the Rebel Alliance Navy. There are also freelance, or privateer, organizations that hire and train pilots, such as various smuggling operations and minor security forces.\n\nBefore arriving here, you made a choice as to which type of organizations you would prefer to join: Imperial, Rebel, or Privateer. You have been provided with a waypoint in your datapad that marks the location of a trainer for the organization you chose. The path to that trainer has also been marked for you, so that you may follow it from the starport to your trainer.\n\nIf you wish to know more about Imperial, Rebel, or Privateer organizations, many of them contact potential recruits such as yourself via email. This correspondence invites you to speak with a coordinator from the organization.  If interested, you might wish to check your email for just such a thing.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 179, 'space_info_how_to_check_email', '[bleep... bloop... whir... whir]\nLook for the flashing ''envelope'' icon on your interface. It''s placed on the lower right-hand side of your screen by default.\n\nDouble-click on the envelope icon, and read your mail.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 180, 'space_info_how_to_travel', '[vweet... plerp... beep... zwing]\nUntil you have your own ship, your options for traveling to a location on the surface of a planet are limited to walking and purchasing a shuttle or starship ticket.\n\nIf you choose to walk to a location on your current planet, I suggest opening your planetary map (ctrl-v) and creating a waypoint at your destination. You can do this by right-clicking on the map at the location that is your target or by right-clicking one of the locations listed on the right-hand side of the map. Either way, choose the option to create a waypoint and one will be added to your datapad.\n\nIf you choose to purchase a shuttle or starport ticket, simply travel to the nearest shuttleport or starport and purchase a ticket from the ticket terminal. Shuttleports are used to travel to destinations on your current planet. Starports are used to travel to different planets, though you may also travel to other locations on the same planet. Once you have your ticket, walk to the ticket droid and present your ticket. The ticket droid will let you know when the next transport will be leaving.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 181, 'space_info_how_to_make_money', '[whir... boop... click... zzt]\nThere are many civilian contracts available on the ''mission terminals'' you find throughout town. Look for them near any major structure. Use the terminal to bring up the current list of local contracts. Choose the one that interests you the most, and you''ll make money when the task is complete.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 182, 'menu_space', 'Starship Pilot Help'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 183, 'space_cannot_call', 'Your helper droid is not built for the pressures of space. Call it when you are on a planet.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 184, 'entertainer_quest_03_sullustan', '[beep... clik... tweetle... clik... whir... zang] \nYour next task was to restyle your hair, but as a Sullustan, you do not have hair or anything else to style. I have been authorized to skip this step and move on to the next one.\n\nBefore I do, I''d like to make sure you know that you can help others style their hair by grouping with them, then targeting them, and then either selecting the Image Design radial menu option or typing /imagedesign. If you progress as an Image Designer, you will eventually learn how to change the style and color your skull markings... among other things.\n\nLet''s move on.'),
('string/en/new_player.stf', 185, 'entertainer_quest_03_ithorian', '[beep... clik... tweetle... clik... whir... zang] \nYour next task was to restyle your hair, but as an Ithorian, you are not yet able to do this. I have been authorized to skip this step and move on to the next one.\n\nBefore I do, I''d like to make sure you know that you can help others style their hair by grouping with them, then targeting them, and then either selecting the Image Design radial menu option or typing /imagedesign. If you progress as an Image Designer, you will eventually learn how to change many aspects of your appearance.\n\nLet''s move on.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 1, 'neutral_dislike_greeting_1', 'Oh, it''s you again.  What do you need now?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 2, 'neutral_neutral_greeting_1', 'Yes?  What can I do for you?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 3, 'neutral_dislike_farewell_1', 'Good riddance!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 4, 'neutral_like_greeting_1', 'Hi there!  How are things going?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 5, 'neutral_neutral_farewell_1', 'Good day to you sir.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 6, 'neutral_like_farewell_1', 'See you later!  Don''t be a stranger.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 7, 'neutral_cry_for_help_1', 'Oh Dear!  Someone help!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 8, 'neutral_cry_warning_1', 'Look out!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 9, 'neutral_loot_1', 'Hmm...this looks interesting.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 10, 'neutral_victory_1', 'Yes!  That''s done!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 11, 'neutral_overhear_name_1', 'Excuse me?  Did you mean me?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 12, 'neutral_like_see_attack_1', 'Hey!  Stop that!  That''s my friend!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 13, 'neutral_neutral_see_attack_1', 'Hey!  What are you doing!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 14, 'neutral_dislike_see_attack_1', 'Hit him harder!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 15, 'neutral_like_see_death_1', 'Oh no!  My friend is dead!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 16, 'neutral_neutral_see_death_1', 'Oh my, what''s happening here?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 17, 'neutral_dislike_see_death_1', 'I never liked that person much anyway.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 18, 'neutral_offer_mission_1', 'Can you do me a small favor?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 19, 'neutral_mission_accepted_1', 'Fantastic.  I''m sure you''ll get it done.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 20, 'neutral_mission_declined_1', 'That''s too bad.  I need to find someone to help me.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 21, 'imperial_dislike_greeting_1', 'What is it?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 22, 'imperial_neutral_greeting_1', 'What can I do for you?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 23, 'imperial_like_greeting_1', 'Good day!  What can I do for you?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 24, 'imperial_cry_for_help_1', 'Guards!  Stormtroopers!  Come quickly!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 25, 'imperial_dislike_farewell_1', 'Be gone from here.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 26, 'imperial_like_farewell_1', 'Good day to you sir.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 27, 'imperial_neutral_farewell_1', 'Good bye.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 28, 'imperial_cry_warning_1', 'Watch out!  '),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 29, 'imperial_dislike_see_attack_1', 'Excellent shot sir.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 30, 'imperial_like_see_attack_1', 'Guards!  Help this man!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 31, 'imperial_neutral_see_attack_1', 'Be more careful, I could have been hurt.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 32, 'imperial_loot_1', 'My superiors will be interested in this.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 33, 'imperial_dislike_see_death_1', 'That''s one less problem to worry about.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 34, 'imperial_like_see_death_1', 'You will be avenged!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 35, 'imperial_neutral_see_death_1', 'How unfortunate.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 36, 'imperial_victory_1', 'Yes!  That was for the Emperor''s glory!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 37, 'imperial_mission_accepted_1', 'Very good.  Now get to work.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 38, 'imperial_mission_declined_1', 'Well, some people just don''t have what it takes.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 39, 'imperial_offer_mission_1', 'Are you ready to do some work for the glory of the empire?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 40, 'imperial_overhear_name_1', 'What did you say?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 41, 'rebel_dislike_greeting_1', 'Oh, it''s you.  What is it now?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 42, 'rebel_like_greeting_1', 'Hey, how are you?  Can I help you with anything?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 43, 'rebel_neutral_greeting_1', 'Hello.  What do you need?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 44, 'rebel_cry_for_help_1', 'I need some backup here!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 45, 'rebel_dislike_farewell_1', 'Get lost.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 46, 'rebel_like_farewell_1', 'May the force be with you.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 47, 'rebel_neutral_farewell_1', 'Good bye.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 48, 'rebel_cry_warning_1', 'Look out!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 49, 'rebel_dislike_see_attack_1', 'I refuse to help you!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 50, 'rebel_like_see_attack_1', 'I''ll get you some help!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 51, 'rebel_neutral_see_attack_1', 'He''s being killed!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 52, 'rebel_loot_1', 'This will help us.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 53, 'rebel_dislike_see_death_1', 'They got what was coming to them.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 54, 'rebel_like_see_death_1', 'Oh, no!  That was my friend!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 55, 'rebel_neutral_see_death_1', 'What a tragedy.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 56, 'rebel_victory_1', 'The Empire will fall!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 57, 'rebel_mission_accepted_1', 'The alliance thanks you for your help.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 58, 'rebel_mission_declined_1', 'That''s too bad.  We could have really used your help.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 59, 'rebel_offer_mission_1', 'Can you do the alliance a small favor?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 60, 'rebel_overhear_name_1', 'Were you talking about me?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 61, 'hutt_dislike_greeting_1', 'I don''t have time for your petty troubles.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 62, 'hutt_like_greeting_1', 'Good to see you.  How are things?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 63, 'hutt_neutral_greeting_1', 'What can you do for me?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 64, 'hutt_cry_for_help_1', 'Help!  I need assistance!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 65, 'hutt_dislike_farewell_1', 'If you come back again I''ll probably kill you.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 66, 'hutt_like_farewell_1', 'Stay out of trouble, friend.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 67, 'hutt_neutral_farewell_1', 'See you.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 68, 'hutt_cry_warning_1', 'Watch it!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 69, 'hutt_dislike_see_attack_1', 'Haha!  That''s what you get.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 70, 'hutt_like_see_attack_1', 'Keep your head down, I''ll try to help!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 71, 'hutt_neutral_see_attack_1', 'None of my business.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 72, 'hutt_loot_1', 'This is good stuff.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 73, 'hutt_dislike_see_death', 'Too bad you can''t bring him back and kill him again.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 74, 'hutt_like_see_death_1', 'Don''t think we''re gonna let you get away with that.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 75, 'hutt_neutral_see_death_1', 'I wonder if I can use this to my advantage somehow.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 76, 'hutt_victory_1', 'Haha!  We win!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 77, 'hutt_mission_accepted_1', 'Good.  Welcome to the team.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 78, 'hutt_mission_declined_1', 'Well, not everyone''s cut out for the life.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 79, 'hutt_offer_mission_1', 'Can you do some work and keep your mouth shut?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 80, 'hutt_overhear_name_1', 'I didn''t do it, whatever you''re talking about.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 81, 'stormtrooper_dislike_greeting_1', 'Let me see your papers.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 82, 'stormtrooper_', ''),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 83, 'stormtrooper_dislike_farewell_1', 'You''re not authorized to be here.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 84, 'stormtrooper_dislike_see_attack_1', 'Blast em!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 85, 'stormtrooper_dislike_see_death_1', 'Enemy down.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 86, 'stormtrooper_like_greeting_1', 'How can I help you?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 87, 'stormtrooper_like_farewell_1', 'So long.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 88, 'stormtrooper_like_see_attack_1', 'Stand aside, I''ll deal with this!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 89, 'stormtrooper_like_see_death_1', 'Friendly down!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 90, 'stormtrooper_neutral_greeting_1', 'Are you authorized to be here?'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 91, 'stormtrooper_neutral_farewell_1', 'Good bye.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 92, 'stormtrooper_neutral_see_attack_1', 'Fighting going on.  I''m waiting for orders...'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 93, 'stormtrooper_neutral_see_death_1', 'Looks like it''s over for now.'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 94, 'stormtrooper_cry_for_help_1', 'I need backup!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 95, 'stormtrooper_cry_warning_1', 'Here they come!'),
('string/en/npc_convo.stf', 96, 'stormtrooper_victory_1', 'Looks like we''ve done it.'),
